    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/accounting-specialist-accounts-receivable-cashiering-manhattan-kansas-united-states-08056cda-1c0e-4dcf-b697-4e50039cfc96": {
      "title": "Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering)",
      "description": "Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Apply Now Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) The position is responsible for all aspects of accounts receivable for the Veterinary Health Center LA section. This position will evaluate client accounts, accept payments, reconcile cash drawers and receipts and assist clients with any account needs necessary. This position will also work with the business manager with any business office accounts receivable along with some possible accounts payable. 522351 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Vet Med Support Services Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 23 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The position is responsible for all aspects of accounts receivable for the Veterinary Health Center LA section. This position will evaluate client accounts, accept payments, reconcile cash drawers and receipts and assist clients with any account needs necessary. This position will also work with the business manager with any business office accounts receivable along with some possible accounts payable. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and six months of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: 1 year of relevant experience Ability to calculate sales and change quickly Accountability and accuracy in reconciling sales receipts Oriented toward serving others and helping clients Exceptional client-service skills Excellent verbal communication Ability to work in a fast-paced, stressful environment Attention to detail Knowledge of point-of-sale systems Bachelor’s degree in business or related field 2-3 years’ experience in cashiering or accounts receivable area 1-2 years’ experience in accounts payable area Ability to speak foreign language, specifically Spanish Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover Letter Resume References Application Window Applications close on: 10/23/2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $ 14.54 - $ 21.81 hourly Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 63ec069c Last Name (required) 95fe8ffc Email (required) 93ac8e5f Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 8d77f5c1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Business / Accounting / Finance Veterinary Medicine Administrative / Professional Business / Accounting / Finance Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) faa5b0c2 Last Name (required) 26b88cbb Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 35af3e36 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 4abe57e7 Last Name (r