    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/accommodations-ada-specialist-or-coordinator-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Accommodations/ADA Specialist or Coordinator",
      "description": "Accommodations/ADA Specialist or Coordinator - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Accommodations/ADA Specialist or Coordinator - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Accommodations/ADA Specialist or Coordinator Apply Now Accommodations/ADA Specialist or Coordinator Reporting to the Director of Employee Relations & Engagement, this position provides guidance and support to employees, supervisors, event guests, 4-H youth program participants, visitors, and applicants across all campuses when health conditions or religious beliefs affect employment, access to campus activities, or the workplace. The role manages the interactive accommodation process for disability and religious accommodation requests, applying the ADA, ADAAA, PWFA, PUMP Act, FMLA, and related state and university policy. 522325 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Human Resources Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Oct 19 2026 - 23:55 CDT Hybrid and/or Remote eligible Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Reporting to the Director of Employee Relations & Engagement, this position provides guidance and support to employees, supervisors, event guests, 4-H youth program participants, visitors, and applicants across all campuses when health conditions or religious beliefs affect employment, access to campus activities, or the workplace. The role manages the interactive accommodation process for disability and religious accommodation requests, applying the ADA, ADAAA, PWFA, PUMP Act, FMLA, and related state and university policy. This posting will be filled at one of two levels , based on the selected candidate's qualifications and experience: • Accommodations Specialist : manages the day-to-day interactive accommodation process and resolves most cases directly, escalating especially complex matters to the Director of ERE/ADA Coordinator for final determination. • Accommodations Coordinator : manages the day-to-day interactive accommodation process and provides independent authority over final accommodation determinations, complaint investigation and resolution, and institution-wide compliance. Duties and Responsibilities (Both Levels): Facilitate the interactive accommodation process, reviewing medical/religious documentation and correspondence to determine reasonable accommodations Maintain confidential case files and produce case management reports and metrics Serve as a resource for supervisors and departmental representatives on accommodation-related questions and processes Develop and deliver training and resource materials on accommodation processes and disability-related topics Support the University's broader ADA compliance and program-development initiatives Proactively partner with Employee Relations, Benefits, and the Time & Leave teams and others on complex employee matters, leveraging a comprehensive understanding of accommodation, leave, benefits, and employee relations considerations to support well-informed and organizationally aligned decisions. Additional Responsibilities at the Coordinator Level: Serve as the University's designated ADA point of contact, with final decision-making authority on the most complex accommodation determinations Receive, investigate, and resolve ADA-related complaints and grievances in accordance with university procedures Interpret evolving federal, state, and local disability law; recommend and implement policy updates Provide oversight, consultation, and escalation support to departmental representatives across campuses Chair or represent the University on relevant accessibility committees and working groups About Us The Division of Human Resources partners with leaders, faculty, and staff across Kansas State University to build a thriving, people-centered workplace that supports the university’s mission of teaching, research, and service. Our team advances initiatives that strengthen the employee experience, promote professional growth, and support a high-performing and engaged workforce. The division includes approximately 50 professionals delivering strategic and operational HR services to the campus community. Key functional areas include ASC-HR, Benefits, Compensation and Organizational Effectiveness, Employee Relations and Engagement, ERP Systems, Resource Center Operations, Talent Acquisition, Talent and Organizational Development, and Time and Leave. Together, these teams partner with campus units to provide responsive HR support, enhance organizational effectiveness, and help attract, develop, and retain a talented workforce. Worksite Description This position is Hybrid and/or Remote eligible . This position works remotely; however, the employee must be in proximity for on-campus meetings that take place throughout the week. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and five years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Human Resources, Rehabilitation Counseling, Social Work, or related field. Knowledge of ADA, ADAAA, PWFA, PUMP Act, FMLA, Workers' Compensation, and related accommodation/leave programs. Strong communication skills across audiences with varying levels of familiarity with the topic. Experience with case management systems and HR/HRIS databases. Candidates with the following qualifications and experience may be considered for the Accommodations Coordinator role: 3–5 years of direct experience in disability services, ADA/504 compliance, or accommodation case management. ADA Coordinator Training Certification Program (ACTCP) completed or in progress. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover letter Resume Three professional references Application Window Applications close on:10/19/2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Accommodations Specialist: $47,486 - $59,500 Accommodations Coordinator : $55,000 - $74,000 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 8de0a712 Last Name (required) 93379312 Email (required) 93609726 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 3beb38d6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Human Resources Human Resources Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite Hybrid and/or Remote eligible Hybrid and/or Remote eligible Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 06004d1f Last Name (required) 5faa7d19 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 122a4726 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 0286106f Last Name (required) 050587b6 Email (required) 60dcb402 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 9bfd9a29 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00