    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/research-technician-manhattan-kansas-united-states-c670e9fa-568e-4c9b-a8bd-01b5dc608187": {
      "title": "Research Technician",
      "description": "Research Technician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Research Technician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Research Technician Apply Now Research Technician Support plant lipid and Drosophila genetics research through routine lab procedures, including DNA extraction, PCR, sample preparation, and plant/insect care, in Biochemistry and Molecular Biophysics. 522374 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Biochem Molecular Biophysics Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 19 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The purpose of this position is to provide reliable technical support for ongoing laboratory research by carrying out routine experimental procedures essential for data generation and project completion. Responsibilities in the Durrett lab include DNA extraction, genotyping, plant growth and maintenance, seed harvesting, and basic lipid analyses, as well as routine laboratory maintenance and support tasks that assist other projects and ensure efficient lab operations. Responsibilities in the Geisbrecht lab include standard molecular biology techniques (DNA extraction, PCR), Drosophila maintenance and husbandry, dissections, and microscopy, in addition to routine laboratory maintenance and support tasks that assist other projects and ensure efficient lab operations. About Us The Department of Biochemistry provides a strong foundation for understanding the molecular basis of biological processes. Our flexible undergraduate and graduate programs prepare students for careers in medicine, agriculture, biotechnology, and other rapidly evolving fields. The department fosters a collaborative community of faculty, graduate assistants (GTAs/GRAs), and students who are committed to research, teaching, and academic excellence. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: • High school diploma (or equivalent) Preferred Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree in biochemistry, biology, or a closely related field • Experience with lipid analysis techniques • Demonstrated experience with basic molecular biology techniques, such as DNA extraction, PCR, and related methods • Experience with plant growth, maintenance, and sample collection in a research setting • Ability to follow written protocols and standard operating procedures with attention to detail • Experience recording and organizing experimental data accurately • Familiarity with basic laboratory safety practices Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Current resume or curriculum vitae Brief cover letter describing relevant experience and interest in the position Contact information for one professional reference Application Window Applications close on: October 19, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $14.90 - $20.11 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 5cbfccb7 Last Name (required) 1934622b Email (required) 7962c6bc Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 0eccbca9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research / Scientific / Grants Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 40e656ee Last Name (required) 5b9c47a1 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 27bd7b95 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 8337a2fb Last Name (required) 88b53147 Email (required) fb366252 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 0e654c48 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While 