    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/lock-system-specialist-manhattan-kansas-united-states-6d4f48ab-90f5-40cb-935a-6e4c11acffa7": {
      "title": "Lock System Specialist",
      "description": "Lock System Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Lock System Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Lock System Specialist Apply Now Lock System Specialist Unlock your potential in a specialized locksmith career with Housing and Dining Services, Facilities Management. Join a skilled team where craftsmanship, problem-solving, customer service, and integrity make a lasting impact. 522368 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Nov 9 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Housing and Dining Services (HDS) seeks a skilled Lock System Specialist to help maintain the safety, security, and functionality of HDS facilities, including residence halls, apartments, dining centers, retail venues, administrative and maintenance buildings. This journeyman-level position installs, inspects, repairs, and maintains mechanical and electronic locking systems, door hardware, closers, and operators. Responsibilities include rekeying and repinning locks; managing building master key systems; cutting keys; maintaining electronic locks and access cards; and accurately documenting keys, lock configurations, repairs, and materials. The position also manages parts inventory, orders supplies, maintains tools and equipment, and produces departmental signage. The ideal candidate brings strong technical skills, attention to detail, problem-solving abilities, and a commitment to protecting university residents, employees, guests, and property. Integrity, professionalism, and respectful interactions are essential to fostering a safe, welcoming environment consistent with the University Principles of Community About Us Housing and Dining Services is a large, self-operated auxiliary department serving more than 5,000 students that call the K-State campus home. This \"home away from home\" meets more than the basic needs of students living with us — we provide affordable, safe and engaging accommodations and services for our residents, while finding unique ways to support them in their academic pursuits. We pride ourselves on taking excellent care of our residents, and that is reflected in our recent Princeton Review rankings. The 2025 Princeton Review ranks us #2 Happiest Students, #2 Best Quality of Life, #8 Best College Residence Halls, and #14 Best Campus Food. YOU can help make our residents and guests feel welcome and comfortable! Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires six months of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Valid driver's license upon employment. Preferred Qualifications: Journey/advanced level experience in locksmithing Effective written and oral communication skills Strong customer service skills Experience with electronic keying systems Demonstrated proficiency with computer technology Additional Role Information: Participation in the standby rotation is a mandatory requirement for this role. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Online application Application Window Applications close on: November 9, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $18.04 - $24.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) acdbfb61 Last Name (required) 93ec1520 Email (required) 605b288d Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: ea957b82 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) a196133c Last Name (required) ac764ce6 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later bc05b628 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) e90e7401 Last Name (required) c70132e8 Email (required) 235dac25 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 326059ec Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent O