      "title": "Communications Project Manager",
      "description": "Communications Project Manager - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Communications Project Manager - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Communications Project Manager Apply Now Communications Project Manager The purpose of the Communications Project Manager is to administer activities associated with the planning and execution of communications, marketing and event projects for the College of Agriculture Dean’s Office. This position will manage project intake, develop creative briefs, establish timelines, coordinate recruitment and stakeholder communication needs, and ensure projects move efficiently from request through completion. The Communications Project Manager will serve as a central point of contact among college leadership, communications staff, campus partners, vendors and contractors while supporting the delivery of high-quality, strategic communications. 522367 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Ag Deans Office & Dir AES Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 25 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The purpose of the Communications Project Manager is to administer activities associated with the planning and execution of communications, marketing and event projects for the College of Agriculture Dean’s Office. This position will manage project intake, develop creative briefs, establish timelines, coordinate recruitment and stakeholder communication needs, and ensure projects move efficiently from request through completion. The Communications Project Manager will serve as a central point of contact among college leadership, communications staff, campus partners, vendors and contractors while supporting the delivery of high-quality, strategic communications. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma (or equivalent) and seven years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Valid driver's license Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in a communications-related field. Experience developing and managing project plans, implementation schedules and resource allocations. Experience working in a communications and marketing agency or similar professional communications environment. Knowledge of current agricultural practices and the land grant mission. Experience developing, implementing, and monitoring organizational brand(s) and ensuring branding consistency. Experience with multi-platform communications, including video production and editing; audio production and editing; photography; desktop publishing using the Adobe Creative Suite. Experience with social media tools, web design, blogging platforms, data reporting tools, analytics, keyword searching and search engine optimization (SEO). Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter 3 Professional References Application Window Applications close on: 10/25/26 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $28.84-$35.38 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) f8d8c4fa Last Name (required) b722acc1 Email (required) 5547571a Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 36c275e9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Agriculture Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Administrative / Professional Agriculture Communications / Public Relations / Market