    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/associate-director-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director",
      "description": "Associate Director - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Associate Director - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Associate Director Apply Now Associate Director Kansas State University (KSU) seeks an Associate Director to support the Sustainable Intensification of Targeted Agricultural Systems Innovation Lab (SITAS-IL). The Associate Director will lead program implementation, technical integration, and performance management of the SITAS-IL. 522360 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Agronomy Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 15 2026 - 23:55 CDT Remote eligible Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Kansas State University (KSU) seeks an Associate Director to support the Sustainable Intensification of Targeted Agricultural Systems Innovation Lab (SITAS-IL). The Associate Director will lead program implementation, technical integration, and performance management of the SITAS-IL. Reporting to the Program Director, the Associate Director will directly supervise the Program Manager and Data Manager, lead implementation of the program-wide Monitoring, Evaluation, and Learning Plan, and coordinate performance and technical integration across the Innovation Consortia, Regional Implementation Hubs, and in-country partners. The Associate Director will ensure that reliable evidence informs program decisions, adaptive management, technology-scaling pathways, partner performance, and accurate and timely reporting to the U.S. Department of State (DOS). About Us Here at the Department of Agronomy, we strive to equip students and industry members with the tools they need to serve our communities and society as a whole through agriculture. Through each facet of our work, we emphasize the importance of sustainable and efficient practices to conserve our resources and protect the land. The Department of Agronomy, together with the Research and Extension Centers, provides statewide leadership for teaching, research, and extension activities in plant breeding, crop production, range science, soil science, and weed sciences and contributes substantially to activities in genetics, water science, and environmental sciences. Kansas State University is located in Manhattan, KS, in the scenic tallgrass prairies of the Flint Hills of NE Kansas. Manhattan is 125 miles west of Kansas City and 50 miles west of Topeka. Kansas State University is the nation’s first land-grant institution and currently enrolls ~24,000 students. Check the local Convention & Visitors Bureau website (http://www.manhattancvb.org/) for more information. Worksite Description This position is Remote eligible . Work may be performed on employer premises, designated assignment location and/or performed fully in a remote capacity. An employee who is working remotely must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a bachelor's degree and five years of relevant experience in international development, agricultural development, monitoring and evaluation, public policy, or related field. Education beyond the minimum degree requirement may count toward required experience if deemed relevant by the hiring manager. The degree requirement ensures candidates possess the advanced theoretical knowledge, specialized methodologies and critical problem-solving skills essential for managing complex research operations and ensuring regulatory compliance. These competencies are typically developed and rigorously validated only through the comprehensive curriculum and intensive experiential learning inherent in a formal degree program. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in international development, agricultural development, monitoring and evaluation, public policy, or a related field. At least 15 years of experience managing complex, multi-country international development programs, focused on agriculture and food security. Experience leading monitoring, evaluation, and learning activities and preparing timely reports for U.S. Government agencies or other major donors. Experience coordinating universities, research institutions, government agencies, private-sector organizations, and implementing partners. Experience supervising professional staff and managing multiple priorities, deadlines, and program challenges. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English. Senior-level experience with USAID, the U.S. Department of State, Feed the Future, or another U.S. Government program. Experience managing large program portfolios, grants, contracts, or subawards. Experience with program evaluations, surveys, adaptive management, and agricultural technology scaling. Experience working with CGIAR (international research centers) organizations, national agricultural research and extension systems, and universities. Knowledge or experience working in SITAS-IL target regions or countries. Willingness to travel internationally to the target countries of the SITAS-IL. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Letter of interest Resume Name, email, and phone number of three professional references Application Window Applications close on: October 15, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $145,000 - $155,000 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 8c6d04fe Last Name (required) dd4e7038 Email (required) b7e462dc Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: d04a97ff Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture Agronomy Research / Scientific / Grants Agriculture Agronomy Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite Remote eligible Remote eligible Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) bc8f323c Last Name (required) 7ba269e2 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later a6c831e0 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) b9dbd37a Last Name (required) c2f6d3c1 Email (required) 2f586ad8 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 5ddd8c8c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparen