    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/communications-marketing-specialist-manhattan-kansas-united-states-fb6bc947-9a5b-40bd-b72b-5198fb7efa15": {
      "title": "Communications & Marketing Specialist",
      "description": "Communications & Marketing Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Communications & Marketing Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Communications & Marketing Specialist Apply Now Communications & Marketing Specialist The Division of Academic Success & Student Affairs is seeking a Communications & Marketing Specialist. The Communications & Marketing Specialist will develop and deploy various communications and marketing assets such as digital media, advertising and promotional materials that will increase visibility and usage of the services provided by the units within the Division. 522336 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Academic Succ & Student Affair Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Oct 28 2026 - 23:55 CDT Hybrid eligible Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Communications & Marketing Specialist supports the work of the Division of Academic Success and Student Affairs by developing and deploying various communications and marketing assets. This includes digital media, advertising, and promotional materials that are part of a strategic and integrated communications plan seeking to increase the visibility and usage of the services, resources and opportunities provided by units within the Division. About Us The Division of Academic Success and Student Affairs supports student professional and personal development inside and outside the classroom by providing impactful opportunities for engagement. Our division is organized around the five areas of academic and career engagement, community building, student belonging, student support and accountability and student well-being. Worksite Description This position is Hybrid eligible . Candidates must be on campus regularly throughout each work week. Hybrid eligibility will be evaluated based on individual performance. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma (or equivalent) Four years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree preferably in art, marketing and communications or related field 1-3 years professional experience Experience with multi-platform communications, including video production and editing, photography and desk top publishing using Adobe Creative Cloud Experience with project management and social media management tools i.e. WorkZone and Sprout Social Experience in client relations Experience with social media and storytelling Ability to work within strict deadlines Effective interpersonal communication skills with a variety of constituencies Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Letter of interest detailing experience as it applies to this position Resume Three professional references with contact information Application Window Applications close on: October 28, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $20.30 - $25.87 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 9e026900 Last Name (required) 8629059c Email (required) 667466dc Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 76305893 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Administrative / Professional Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite Hybrid eligible Hybrid eligible Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 58f196ba Last Name (required) f0170457 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 3339557c Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 6c0a55c2 Last Name (required) 8fa58329 Email (required) 183af349 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 0707e6b6 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparen