    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/office-specialist-v-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Office Specialist V",
      "description": "Office Specialist V - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Office Specialist V - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Office Specialist V Apply Now Office Specialist V This position provides the highest-level administrative associate support to the Department of Grain and Food Science (GFS) and its department head in carrying forward the activities of the department. GFS is a complex department which includes four undergraduate and four graduate degree programs, research, and extension in both grain and food sciences, and is home to the International Grains Program Institute. These comprehensive efforts are supported by over 50 faculty and staff employees located in between main campus and north campus in one of our four facilities off Kimball. This position is the focal point of activities for many of these efforts internally and often serves as the first point of contact for many stakeholders, alumni, supporters and students in Grain Science and Food Science. 522346 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Grain and Food Science Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 25 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position provides the highest-level administrative associate support to the Department of Grain and Food Science (GFS) and its department head in carrying forward the activities of the department. GFS is a complex department which includes four undergraduate and four graduate degree programs, research, and extension in both grain and food sciences, and is home to the International Grains Program Institute. These comprehensive efforts are supported by over 50 faculty and staff employees located in between main campus and north campus in one of our four facilities off Kimball. This position is the focal point of activities for many of these efforts internally and often serves as the first point of contact for many stakeholders, alumni, supporters and students in Grain Science and Food Science. About Us The Department of Grain and Food Science is committed to providing high-quality education, advancing innovation in grain and food science research, and building strong industry partnerships to meet the evolving needs of global food systems. Our faculty includes several current and former Grain and Food Science members who are ranked among the world’s top 2% of researchers in a 2020 Stanford University study. For more than 110 years, Kansas State University has been a global leader in flour milling and industry-focused education. Since 1951, it has remained one of the few institutions worldwide to offer four-year bachelor’s degrees in Bakery Science and Management, Feed and Pet Food Science, Food Science, and Milling Science and Management. Our internationally recognized graduate program also provides a wide range of opportunities for both applied and fundamental research, leading to master’s and doctoral degrees in grain science, food science, and related fields. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires four years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: A Bachelor’s degree in any discipline, particularly business management and/or communications is highly preferred. Experience in administrative/programmatic support, coordination for an administrator, scheduling/calendar management, support for events, meetings, and communication support. High proficiency with technology, including skills with Microsoft Office suite (specifically word, excel, online calendaring, scheduling) Excellent oral and written communication skills. Demonstrated ability to exercise judgment and discretion and maintain integrity with sensitive or confidential information. Demonstrated problem solving and analytical skills, including the ability to research and analyze administrative problems, make recommendations, and take appropriate courses of action. Ability to be flexible, innovative, and receptive to taking on new or changing responsibilities. Ability to work independently or as a member of a team with accountability for results. Excellent organizational skills with ability to manage multiple priorities concurrently and pay attention to accuracy, detail and follow through. Customer service orientation and strong interpersonal skills including courtesy, professionalism, and a cooperative attitude. Proven ability to interact effectively in a multicultural environment with a wide variety of stakeholders. Working knowledge of university policies and procedures. Supervisory skills. Ability to take initiative and make difficult decisions. Event planning experience. Additional Role Information: Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. KSU Page UP online application 2. Letter of Interest 3. Resume 4. List of three references with email addresses and phone numbers listed Application Window Applications close on: October 25, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range 42,216.00 - 65,000.00 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 220a6d4a Last Name (required) f0547e65 Email (required) 6de46f0a Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 8dcac3a9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Agriculture Business / Accounting / Finance Food Safety / Science / Systems Administrative / Professional Agriculture Business / Accounting / Finance Food Safety / Science / Systems Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 74cd24c4 Last Name (required) d0619060 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 91d3911c Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 673e857c Last Name (required) 96065739 Email (required) b920c529 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 94be90f9 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 