    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/fellow-post-doc-manhattan-kansas-united-states-467a1a2e-3527-4efe-b43f-6ebef65a858b": {
      "title": "Fellow (Post Doc)",
      "description": "Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Fellow (Post Doc) Apply Now Fellow (Post Doc) The Liu laboratory in the Plant Pathology department at Kansas State University seeks a highly motivated candidate interested in research projects related to crop genetics and genomics. 522343 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Plant Pathology Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Nov 1 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Liu laboratory in the Plant Pathology department at Kansas State University seeks a highly motivated candidate interested in research projects related to crop genetics and genomics. The ideal candidate is expected to have excellent technical skills in bioinformatics. Specifically, The position will lead genome assembly, comparative genomics, and population genetics analyses to uncover the genetic basis of sugar biosynthesis in sugar beet. The position will also involve developing computational tools and analytical pipelines to support genetic and genomic research. Self-guidance and resourcefulness are necessary qualities for success in the position. The Liu Lab is currently supported by both the NSF, USDA, and DOE on research projects, including plant disease resistance, plant regeneration, and genomic analysis for both plants and pathogens. More project information can be found at the lab website: https://liu3zhenlab.github.io/. About Us The Department of Plant Pathology at Kansas State University comprises a large and varying group of scientists with excellent reputations in research, teaching, and extension. Our strengths are in applied plant pathology, microbiology, biosecurity, disease diagnosis, management, host-parasite resistance genetics, pathogen and microbe genetics and genomics, genomics and biotechnology. Kansas State University is located in Manhattan, KS, in the scenic tallgrass prairies of the Flint Hills of NE Kansas. Manhattan is 125 miles west of Kansas City and 50 miles west of Topeka. Kansas State University is the nation’s first land-grant institution and currently enrolls ~24,000 students. Check the local Convention & Visitors Bureau website (http://www.manhattancvb.org/) for more information. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in molecular biology, plant genetics, computational biology, or related fields. The degree requirement is necessary to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Demonstrated proficiency in programming, particularly in Python. Strong publication record in peer-reviewed journals Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge in molecular biology, genetics, and bioinformatics. Sponsorship eligibility: This position is eligible for sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Letter of Interest 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Name, email and phone number for three professional references Application Window Applications close on: November 1, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $53,000-$60,000 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 60b0f75d Last Name (required) 006f77a7 Email (required) ecdd74ea Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 2da0f065 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture Plant Sciences Research / Scientific / Grants Agriculture Plant Sciences Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 79a0eb16 Last Name (required) 0da98af4 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later b1a1f1d0 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) b3c43981 Last Name (required) 54c5374b Email (required) c5bdf4b9 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job afc77a5c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shado