    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/financial-aid-specialist-manhattan-kansas-united-states-4084b12c-e262-4391-b1ce-8594b8515e3d": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Specialist",
      "description": "Financial Aid Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Financial Aid Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Financial Aid Specialist Apply Now Financial Aid Specialist The Office of Student Financial Assistance seeks individuals interested in joining our processing team. This position administers key federal and institutional financial aid programs, including Federal Work-Study, Kansas Career Work-Study, tuition assistance, Return to Title IV, and federal aid awarding. The role ensures student eligibility, accurate and timely awards, fiscal accountability, regulatory compliance, and effective communication with students, employees, employers, and university partners. The position also provides guidance on program requirements, analyzes student and financial aid data, and supports the successful administration of financial aid throughout the academic year. 522345 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Student Financial Assistance Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Oct 23 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position has a very similar counterpart position which comprises part of our processing unit. The processing unit ensures that all the behind-the-scenes tasks are being completed in an efficient and timely manner. Several aspects of this position involve the application, awarding and administration of federal, state, and institutional aid programs. The incumbent reviews eligibility criteria for the aid programs, awards where appropriate, communicates with applicable individuals, and ensures proper management of the funds is maintained. The Return to Title IV (R2T4) aspects of this position are very complex and time sensitive. Certain functions within the position have mandated timeframes in which tasks must be completed to maintain institutional compliance with Federal Student Aid regulations. Ensuring compliance and following university and office policies and procedures is necessary. About Us The staff members in the Office of Student Financial Assistance serve students and their families at every step of the journey while at Kansas State University to guide students through the scholarship and financial aid process. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma (or equivalent) 3 years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Associates degree or higher 9 or more months work experience in a student financial aid office. 12 or more months work experience performing accounting, budgeting, finance or banking related tasks. Able to research, analyze, interpret, and explain complex regulations and/or policies. Effective verbal and written communication to enhance exemplary customer service skills. Previous work experience utilizing comprehensive student information system or similar technology. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional Reference Application Window Applications close on: October 23,2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $ 18.04 - $23.00 Hourly Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) e47e1378 Last Name (required) 39373e3d Email (required) 4c5ad6ed Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 50ee0d7e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Business / Accounting / Finance Student Affairs / Services Administrative / Professional Business / Accounting / Finance Student Affairs / Services Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) c200e2d4 Last Name (required) 0a01a254 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 2c369b5b Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 131320c1 Last Name (required) 44c757e8 Email (required) 92c5086f Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 7b185fff Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job’s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate’s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State’s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) db68c703 Last Name (required) c94aca5a Email (required) 316baafd Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 