    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/fellow-post-doc-manhattan-kansas-united-states-d1a31ca2-8a4d-4d4f-bc67-09a48caf609f": {
      "title": "Fellow (Post Doc)",
      "description": "Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Fellow (Post Doc) Apply Now Fellow (Post Doc) To conduct and lead research in companion animal nutrition and metabolism, with a focus on, but not limited to, protein and energy metabolism in domestic cats. The position will coordinate feeding trails, develop research methods, conduct laboratory and statistical analyses, prepare scientific publications and reports, contribute to grant proposals, and help mentor graduate students. 522330 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Grain and Food Science Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 13 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role To conduct and lead research in companion animal nutrition and metabolism, with a focus on, but not limited to, protein and energy metabolism in domestic cats. The position will coordinate feeding trails, develop research methods, conduct laboratory and statistical analyses, prepare scientific publications and reports, contribute to grant proposals, and help mentor graduate students. About Us The Department of Grain and Food Science is committed to providing high-quality education, advancing innovation in grain and food science research, and building strong industry partnerships to meet the evolving needs of global food systems. Our faculty includes several current and former Grain and Food Science members who are ranked among the world’s top 2% of researchers in a 2020 Stanford University study. For more than 110 years, Kansas State University has been a global leader in flour milling and industry-focused education. Since 1951, it has remained one of the few institutions worldwide to offer four-year bachelor’s degrees in Bakery Science and Management, Feed and Pet Food Science, Food Science, and Milling Science and Management. Our internationally recognized graduate program also provides a wide range of opportunities for both applied and fundamental research, leading to master’s and doctoral degrees in grain science, food science, and related fields. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: • Ph.D. in Animal Science, Veterinary Medicine, Biochemistry, Nutrition, or a related discipline. The degree requirement is necessary to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: • Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a research team. • Ability to manage multiple responsibilities, troubleshoot technical issues, and develop and execute detailed research protocols. • Strong scientific writing skills, including a record of peer-reviewed publications. • Hands-on experience working with domestic cats. • Experience with indirect calorimetry, stable isotope techniques and/or protein and energy metabolism research. • Knowledge of feline behavior. • Excellent oral and written communication skills Additional Role Information: Sponsorship eligibility: This position is eligible for sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Resume 2. Letter of Interest 3. List of three references with email addresses and phone numbers listed Application Window Applications close on:10/13/2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $48,000.00 - $55,000.00 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 55a3bd99 Last Name (required) 2c56a4b2 Email (required) a6635c8b Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 1be02941 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture Food Safety / Science / Systems Health & Safety Nutrition Research / Scientific / Grants Agriculture Food Safety / Science / Systems Health & Safety Nutrition Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 2d9b2085 Last Name (required) 3340406c Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 057b1661 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) bc32a1ec Last Name (required) 65e8a1ae Email (required) 83f6500e Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 342953ef Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Bl