    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/fire-inspector-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Fire Inspector",
      "description": "Fire Inspector - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fire Inspector - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Fire Inspector Apply Now Fire Inspector The position performs required inspections and testing of fire emergency equipment in compliance with state adopted fire codes. The position assists with assurance measures for other applicable State and Federal regulations and titles affecting higher education institutions. Position provides assistance with cursory inspection of key areas in compliance with regulations for life safety, occupational safety and health, and environmental protection, but the position's primary role is required in response to stipulations of the international fire code and additional fire safety requirements mandated by the State of Kansas. This position will assist senior personnel with ensuring environmental and industrial safety compliance assurance and laboratory safety by providing information during fire equipment inspections of key areas of concern and/or non-compliance to safety protocol to ensure that K-State is meeting Federal, State, local codes and regulations, and the expectations of accrediting bodies and funding entities as they pertain to environmental and safety matters 522338 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Environmental Health & Safety Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The position performs required inspections and testing of fire emergency equipment in compliance with state adopted fire codes. The position assists with assurance measures for other applicable State and Federal regulations and titles affecting higher education institutions. Position provides assistance with cursory inspection of key areas in compliance with regulations for life safety, occupational safety and health, and environmental protection, but the position's primarily role is required in response stipulations of the international fire code and additional fire safety requirements mandated by the State of Kansas. This position will assist senior personnel with ensuring environmental and industrial safety compliance assurance and laboratory safety by providing information during fire equipment inspections of key areas of concern and/or non-compliance to safety protocol to ensure that K-State is meeting Federal, State, local codes and regulations, and the expectations of accrediting bodies and funding entities as they pertain to environmental and safety matters. About Us The position performs required inspections and testing of fire emergency equipment in compliance with state adopted fire codes. The position assists with assurance measures for other applicable State and Federal regulations and titles affecting higher education institutions. Position provides assistance with cursory inspection of key areas in compliance with regulations for life safety, occupational safety and health, and environmental protection, but the position's primarily role is required in response stipulations of the international fire code and additional fire safety requirements mandated by the State of Kansas. This position will assist senior personnel with ensuring environmental and industrial safety compliance assurance and laboratory safety by providing information during fire equipment inspections of key areas of concern and/or non-compliance to safety protocol to ensure that K-State is meeting Federal, State, local codes and regulations, and the expectations of accrediting bodies and funding entities as they pertain to environmental and safety matters. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires two years of relevant experience and Fire Inspector I certification. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: High School diploma or equivalent. Experience reading and interpreting fire code. Experience conducting building emergency system testing as described in the position duties. Familiarity with fire and life system systems. Basic experience with building electrical systems. Current 40 HazWoper certification. Experience in a higher education setting. Basic computer skills - (i.e., ability to use PC, laptops, tablets, and handheld barcode or other scanners. Able to download data from these systems. Able to use databases for entry and data look up. Able to communicate via email). Demonstrated verbal communication skills and excellent interpersonal skills. Self-motivated and able to work autonomously to complete required testing and inspection. Education or training in electrical/mechanical systems. Additional Role Information: Respond as needed for the Emergency Response Team. Post offer/pre-employment medical evaluation to assess and verify fitness for assigned duties (ability to climb and carry ladders and physical demands as described herein (i.e., physical demands section). Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover Letter Resume 3 References Application Window Applications close on: 11/06/2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $20.30 - $25.87/hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 29c74350 Last Name (required) 65449de8 Email (required) 9ddeac79 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 4dc90941 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health & Safety Health & Safety Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 573814bd Last Name (required) f40a2f6e Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 2c32d2bc Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) f0a4ef1e Last Name (required) 0d79f032 Email (required) ce9f18d9 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job b94c2bb8 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style 