    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/veterinary-assistant-small-animal-icu-manhattan-kansas-united-states-3ca6fe62-fbf2-4e88-ad8f-8c2b38088f78": {
      "title": "Veterinary Assistant - Small Animal ICU",
      "description": "Veterinary Assistant - Small Animal ICU - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Assistant - Small Animal ICU - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Veterinary Assistant - Small Animal ICU Apply Now Veterinary Assistant - Small Animal ICU The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking a Veterinary Assistant to join our dedicated Small Animal ICU team to help facilitate exemplary patient care. Though there are many responsibilities of someone in this position, the primary responsibility is to provide clinical assistance to the ICU staff in the day-to-day operations of caring for critical patients. Individuals in this role will also provide meaningful support through maintaining inventory, organizing necessary equipment, and engaging in basic aspects of patient care. This position prioritizes effective communication and leadership skills daily. Working hours for this position will be Sunday-Tuesday, 3pm-3am. 522333 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Health Center Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 23 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking a Veterinary Assistant to join our dedicated Small Animal ICU team to help facilitate exemplary patient care. Though there are many responsibilities of someone in this position, the primary responsibility is to provide clinical assistance to the ICU staff in the day-to-day operations of caring for critical patients. Individuals in this role will also provide meaningful support through maintaining inventory, organizing necessary equipment, and engaging in basic aspects of patient care. This position prioritizes effective communication and leadership skills daily. Working hours for this position will be Sunday-Tuesday, 3pm-3am. About Us The Veterinary Health Center is a teaching hospital that offers routine, emergency, and specialty care services. The VHC strives to provide exceptional care for patients from high-quality routine healthcare to state-of-the-art advanced therapy for seriously ill patients. The Veterinary Health Center is located in Manhattan, Kansas which is a vibrant college community with a population of over 55,000 in the Flint Hills. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes 24 vacation days plus other paid time off (holidays, sick, and discretionary), health insurance, life insurance, and retirement plans. To see what benefits are available, please visit: www.ksvhc.org/about/employment/recruitment.html Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) One year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Two or more years of experience as a veterinary assistant providing patient care. Ability to work with and provide preventative maintenance for ordinary medical equipment. Ability to handle, restrain, and provide medical treatments to domestic animals. Willingness to master new techniques. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter 3. Contact information for three professional references Application Window Applications close on: 10/23/2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $16.10 - $16.50 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 2c58b14d Last Name (required) c241f257 Email (required) a9672eb3 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: e5b0cb62 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) df783e06 Last Name (required) e0a37ae5 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later f60641f6 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 9bd89c1b Last Name (required) 53ca6d67 Email (required) b72ae5fd Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 0d482532 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Ca