    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/regional-community-vitality-extension-specialist-other-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Regional Community Vitality Extension Specialist",
      "description": "Regional Community Vitality Extension Specialist - Other, Kansas, United States Regional Community Vitality Extension Specialist - Other, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Regional Community Vitality Extension Specialist Apply Now Regional Community Vitality Extension Specialist K-State Extension seeks a Regional Community Vitality Extension Specialist in Phillipsburg to provide community coaching, leadership, strategic guidance and support to Extension professionals, local units and community leaders. 522327 Other Extension Programs Academic / Faculty - 12 month Closing at: Oct 23 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Kansas State University Extension Programs is seeking a Regional Community Vitality Extension Specialist focused on Community Coaching. Based in Phillipsburg at the Huck Boyd Community Center, this specialist will shape the regional coaching ecosystem by providing transformational leadership, strategic guidance, and technical support for Extension professionals, local units, coalitions, and community leaders. The specialist will serve as a connector between grassroots community efforts, local Extension offices, and campus partners. They will champion evidence-informed coaching models that equip community organizations and emerging initiatives to build local capacity from grassroots beginnings through long-term organizational sustainability. Roles and Responsibilities Statewide Curriculum, Training & Resource Development Team Leadership : Establish and lead a specialized Community Coaching Team consisting of local unit agents, regional specialists, and campus partners to develop a robust, statewide coaching curriculum adhering to K-State publication standards. Resource Creation : Create practical, highly accessible community tools, diagnostic guides, and training modules designed for use by communities of varying capacity, including rural towns, underserved groups, and emerging coalitions. Agent & Volunteer Development : In collaboration with system-wide volunteer specialists and local agents, design and lead structured professional development on volunteer recruitment, onboarding, retention, volunteer management, succession planning, and board/coalition leadership. Framework Instruction : Apply and teach evidence-informed community development approaches, including appreciative inquiry, community capitals, and other asset-based frameworks. Regional Community Coaching, Field Support & Programming Core Community Coaching : Coach Extension professionals, community coalitions, and civic leaders through community assessment, visioning, goal setting, strategic planning, initiative implementation, evaluation, and long-term sustainability. Local Unit Collaboration : Partner directly with local Extension units through both in-person and remote coaching to proactively identify and address regional programming gaps via stakeholder-driven networks and localized initiatives. Program Implementation : Guide regional local units through all state-level Community Vitality program rollouts, facilitation frameworks, and coalition-building processes. Impact Evaluation & Data : Facilitate and streamline the collection of community coaching data, utilizing Program Evaluation and Reporting System (PEARS) reporting alongside community feedback and stakeholder input to demonstrate measurable impact and continually refine programming. Partnerships, Sustainability & Professional Development Strategic Partnerships : Actively engage in regional and statewide networking to build multi-sector collaborations and expand programming across the region. Multi-Dimensional Sustainability : Support local units and regional initiatives in building long-term community ownership, leadership pipelines, cross-sector partnerships, and organizational resilience. External Funding Support : Identify and pursue appropriate grant, partnership, and cost-recovery opportunities that support sustainable programming, assisting local units with grant readiness and extramural proposal development. Credentialing & Field Presence : Maintain active coaching credentials, participate in statewide Extension teams, and maintain a visible, engaged presence across regional communities. About Us K-State Extension improves Kansans' lives, livelihoods and communities through education, research, engagement and leadership. With scientists, educators and volunteers in each of the state's 105 counties, our professionals strive to make the university's research and scientific accomplishments accessible and relevant to every household. Worksite Description This position is On-site . Specialists will live and work in their designated region. This position requires regular travel throughout the region to deliver in-person community coaching, support local unit activities, and attend evening and weekend community meetings as appropriate, balanced with remote delivery tools. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: A master’s degree in community development, public administration, sociology, economics, education, organizational leadership, communications, rural sociology, or a closely related field appropriate to the position (or equivalent relevant professional experience where permitted by university policy). Excellent verbal and written English communication skills. Demonstrated ability to design, deliver, facilitate, and evaluate community-based educational initiatives and shared community goals. Demonstrated experience leading collaborative teams, coaching professionals, and facilitating structured professional development. Demonstrated proficiency utilizing electronic communications, virtual meeting tools, educational technology, and data management systems necessary for program delivery and evaluation. Proven commitment to uplifting rural America, with a demonstrated ability to work effectively with rural audiences. Demonstrated track record of building and sustaining partnerships with external community organizations, local agencies, and civic leaders. The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated understanding of or professional experience working within Cooperative Extension, community-based adult education, or outreach-focused institutions. Prior formal training or documented experience in asset-based community development, appreciative inquiry, coaching models, or community capitals frameworks. Demonstrated experience in volunteer management, volunteer coordination, and leadership development. Demonstrated success in extramural grant writing, cost-recovery initiatives, or securing partnership resources. Ph.D. or terminal degree in a discipline related to community vitality, organizational development, or adult education. Additional Role Information: Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. Valid driver’s license at the time of employment. Willingness and ability to travel across the assigned multi-county region and work occasional evenings or weekends as required by community meetings and programming schedules. Official primary office located in Phillipsburg, Kansas. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover Letter: Detailing your professional experience related to community coaching, team leadership, curriculum development, and regional field delivery. Curriculum Vitae / Resume: Highlighting relevant career accomplishments, education, and credentials. Statement of Vision: A brief statement (1–2 pages) outlining your strategic vision for establishing and sustaining a regional community coaching ecosystem across diverse communities. Transcripts: Copies of graduate transcripts for all completed university degrees (official transcripts required upon hire). References: Names, professional titles, email addresses, and phone numbers for three professional references familiar with your direct work history. Application Window Applications close on: October 23, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Commensurate with experience and education. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) c51f1408 Last Name (required) 0372266b Email (required) 5c5bcdbb Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: e44ad2b4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Adult Development Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Community Development / Community Vitality Education / Instructional Extension Agent / Educator Administrative / Professional Adult Development Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Community Development / Community Vitality Education / Instructional Extension Agent / Educator Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 12 month Academic / Faculty - 12 month Locations Other, Kansas, United States Other, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 9af67d70 Last Name (required) 46826702 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later edd7f42f Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 3f6d0c4e Last Name (required) 4feecd6e Email (required) 7c165253 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 9220c954 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job’s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate’s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State’s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) b1d6aae5 Last Name (required) c078bcac Email (required) d6b2ba6f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) e5da76fc Last Name (required) 3ebc875c Email (required) 2b11ddbd Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"
