    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/cook-manhattan-kansas-united-states-f5497f60-cba2-4d8d-b7d8-520183e21c1f": {
      "title": "Cook",
      "description": "Cook - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Cook - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Cook Apply Now Cook Join a great team with great benefits and a tradition of culinary excellence. K-State food has again landed in the Top 20 nationwide. The Princeton Review's \" The Best 390 Colleges \" ranked K-State's campus food at #14 in its 2025 issue. 522264 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 21 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role At the heart of it all, our dynamic team works together to prepare safe, wholesome food for the residents and guests in the Residence Hall system at Kansas State University. Cooks provide food production support to several different food and service platforms in a “from scratch” production environment. The 40 hour per week work schedule includes a generous benefit package. The work schedule includes one Saturday or Sunday (one day) every other weekend. A day off will be scheduled either before or after the weekend day. Duties include: • Prepare multi-step, complex entrees and side dishes using standardized menus and recipes. Assist in the coordination of food production using batch cooking methods. • Operate, clean, and maintain equipment and work areas in a safe and sanitary manner. Comply with all cleaning and sanitation standards. • Evaluate HACCP and food safety activities and works closely with others to make sure all equipment and cleaning standards are being met. Store and handle food in a safe and sanitary manner using established procedures. • Participate as an effective team worker by cooperating with and assisting co-workers and by participating in daily meetings. • Train and oversee the work of student employees in production area. About Us Housing and Dining Services is a large, complex, self-operated auxiliary department employing about 1,000 full and part-time staff. As a diverse group, we share the desire to provide exemplary services, products and facilities for our residents and other guests. K-State food has once again landed in the Top 20 nationwide. The Princeton Review's \" The Best 390 Colleges \" has ranked K-State's campus food at No. 14 in its 2025 issue. It's pretty rare for campus meals to be made from scratch on location, and our students appreciate that! Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires one year of relevant experience in commercial/institutional cooking. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Ability to learn to perform basic math computations to accurately weigh and measure ingredients Ability to use and care for equipment Ability to handle food safely while preparing high quality products. Considerable knowledge of large scale food preparation, equipment, health sanitation, and safety procedures. One to three years experience in an institutional or volume setting. Ability to understand and follow written and oral instructions. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: on-line application Application Window Applications close on: October 21, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $16.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 00e48783 Last Name (required) a41c6f30 Email (required) 74766d5e Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 88d5e5ec Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Dining / Hospitality Food Safety / Science / Systems Dining / Hospitality Food Safety / Science / Systems Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) fea1ed45 Last Name (required) 42df4015 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 885a7f58 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 62190675 Last Name (required) 72e229cc Email (required) 4602b710 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 33025ca4 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transpare