    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/client-services-assistant-manhattan-kansas-united-states-f7907089-3d44-4244-babe-eed19ee1aefd": {
      "title": "Client Services Assistant",
      "description": "Client Services Assistant - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Client Services Assistant - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Client Services Assistant Apply Now Client Services Assistant The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking an overnight Client Services Assistant to join our dedicated team to help facilitate exemplary patient care and quality customer service. Client Services Assistants provide exceptional customer service through taking calls from clients, listening to client needs, and providing helpful solutions to any concerns or issues. Excellent communication skills and critical thinking are utilized daily as this position works during emergency hours and acts as a liaison between clients, patients, and the hospital service providers. Working hours for this position will be 30 hours/week: Friday, Saturday, and Sunday, from 10pm-8am. 522259 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Health Center Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 20 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking an overnight Client Services Assistant to join our dedicated team to help facilitate exemplary patient care and quality customer service. Client Services Assistants provide exceptional customer service through taking calls from clients, listening to client needs, and providing helpful solutions to any concerns or issues. Excellent communication skills and critical thinking are utilized daily as this position works during emergency hours and acts as a liaison between clients, patients, and the hospital service providers. Working hours for this position will be 30 hours/week: Friday, Saturday, and Sunday, from 10pm-8am. About Us The Veterinary Health Center is a teaching hospital that offers routine, emergency, and specialty care services. The VHC strives to provide exceptional care for patients from high-quality routine healthcare to state-of-the-art advanced therapy for seriously ill patients. The Veterinary Health Center is located in Manhattan, Kansas which is a vibrant college community with a population of over 55,000 in the Flint Hills. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes 24 vacation days plus other paid time off (holidays, sick, and discretionary), health insurance, life insurance, and retirement plans. To see what benefits are available, please visit: www.ksvhc.org/about/employment/recruitment.html Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) One year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree or at least two years of post-high school experience. Two years experience in clerical or office support work preferred. Training in general office practice. Experience with veterinary hospital management program software, such as Instinct, will be an asset for this position. Good public relations skills, including the ability to communicate professionally under stress. Working knowledge of medical terminology. Computer skills, including knowledge of work processing computer software and medical data base programs. Ability and skills to efficiently coordinate calls on a multi-line telephone system. Ability to collaborate with established procedures, protocol and instruction from supervisor. Ability to complete data entry in computer system accurately and in a timely fashion. Ability to apply skills of a service-oriented nature position to the public, faculty and students in order to promote harmonious working relationships and excellent veterinary medical care for patients. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter 3. Contact information for three professional references Application Window Applications close: October 20, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $16.50-17.50 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 31d28009 Last Name (required) b3a3abd7 Email (required) d7853aac Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: cea2f853 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Veterinary Medicine Administrative / Professional Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) cf7a10c0 Last Name (required) 6a64c876 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later e6ad48dc Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) f02142b9 Last Name (required) 64d504f2 Email (required) 91163698 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 9e5f46f8 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of In