    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/fellow-post-doc-manhattan-kansas-united-states-e6d6a170-5e1c-406b-84d9-dc5e52661f0c": {
      "title": "Fellow (Post Doc)",
      "description": "Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Fellow (Post Doc) Apply Now Fellow (Post Doc) The postdoctoral position will study cyclic-di-GMP (c-di-GMP) signaling and its role in bacterial virulence. The project will investigate the molecular mechanisms by which c-di-GMP signaling networks regulate sporulation, toxin production, and biofilm formation in the anaerobic bacterial pathogen Clostridioides difficile. The research will utilize a combination of biochemical and genetic approaches to better understand these regulatory mechanisms. 522142 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Biology Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 15 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Division of Biology is seeking a motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to join the lab of Revathi Govind to study cyclic-di-GMP (c-di-GMP) signaling and its role in bacterial virulence. The project will investigate the molecular mechanisms by which c-di-GMP networks control sporulation, toxin production, and biofilm formation in the anaerobic bacterial pathogen Clostridioides difficile, using both biochemical and genetic approaches. About Us The Division of Biology at Kansas State University is composed of a dynamic group of tenure-track, research, and instructional faculty, as well as a large number of postdoctoral research associates, graduate students, and support staff. All of these individuals are essential to accomplish the Division of Biology’s mission, to generate and disseminate high-quality biological scientific knowledge through teaching, research, service, and outreach. The research, teaching, and service interests of these individuals, spanning all areas of biological research, teaching and training at the postdoctoral, graduate, and undergraduate levels, as well as service and outreach contributions to the broader scientific community and the public. Worksite Description This position is On-site . N/A All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: • PhD in Microbiology, Molecular Biology, Biochemistry, or a related field (completed or near completion) • Experience with bacterial genetics (creating and screening mutants, various cloning methods, PCR, qRT-PCR, protein expression and purification, RNA-seq and general microbiology techniques. • Strong written and verbal communication skills • Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment Preferred Qualifications: • Prior experience with bacterial pathogens • Familiarity with high throughput sequencing and bioinformatics Additional Role Information: • Design and execute experiments • Analyze and interpret data, and contribute to manuscript preparation • Present findings at lab meetings and scientific conferences • Mentor graduate and undergraduate students as needed Sponsorship eligibility: This position is eligible for sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: CV Brief statement of research interests Contact information for three references to rgovind@ksu.edu. Application Window Applications close on: October 15, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $56,000 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 93ba4d94 Last Name (required) 7d857cae Email (required) f3222dc3 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 4a2dbf88 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research / Scientific / Grants Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff 