    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/vet-nurse-ii-small-animal-emergency-manhattan-kansas-united-states-8092d26d-cd74-4503-b322-a3ae3db35bd5": {
      "title": "Vet Nurse II-Small Animal Emergency",
      "description": "Vet Nurse II-Small Animal Emergency - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Vet Nurse II-Small Animal Emergency - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Vet Nurse II-Small Animal Emergency Apply Now Vet Nurse II-Small Animal Emergency This position provides veterinary support and performs semi-routine tasks in the Small Animal Emergency Care section of the Veterinary Health Center at Kansas State University. Employee provides assistance in the care of patients through independently performing technical procedures and administering treatments. Other responsibilities include training of students and employees on various tasks, monitoring medical records, and collaboration with colleagues to meet patient care standards. 521477 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Health Center Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 28 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking a Veterinary Nurse to join our dedicated Small Animal Emergency team to help facilitate exemplary patient care and quality customer service. This employee provides assistance in the care of patients through independently performing technical procedures and administering treatments. Other responsibilities include training of students and employees on various tasks, monitoring medical records, and collaboration with colleagues to meet patient care standards. Shifts for this position may vary depending on department needs, however, typical working hours will include Friday and Monday 12am-8am, Saturday and Sunday 12am-12pm. About Us The Veterinary Health Center is a teaching hospital that offers routine, emergency, and specialty care services. The VHC strives to provide exceptional care for patients from high-quality routine healthcare to state-of-the-art advanced therapy for seriously ill patients. The Veterinary Health Center is located in Manhattan, Kansas which is a vibrant college community with a population of over 55,000 in the Flint Hills. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes 24 vacation days plus other paid time off (holidays, sick, and discretionary), health insurance, life insurance, and retirement plans. To see what benefits are available, please visit: www.ksvhc.org/about/employment/recruitment.html Worksite Option This position is required to be performed on-site . Work is performed on employer premises or designated assignment location. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Completion of a two-year college program in veterinary or animal technology accredited by the American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA). Two years of relevant experience. Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of basic veterinary medical concepts, animal behavior and animal husbandry. Advanced knowledge of nursing care, service flow, and section requirements. Ability to handle, restrain, and provide medical treatments to domestic animals. Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others. Ability to perform diagnostic procedures. Ability to work with and provide preventative maintenance for ordinary veterinary medical hospital equipment. Ability to adhere to appropriate safety procedures. Ability to work in high intensity environment. Skilled in time management and prioritizing daily tasks. Skilled in interpersonal communication, written and oral. Skilled in basic computer skills. Ability to train other employees. Be willing to master new techniques. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Contact information for three professional references Application Window Closes October 28, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $22.00-24.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) f6e1a8d5 Last Name (required) 6e2ffb53 Email (required) 41ca6aa0 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: e1cd6e46 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 5a40b178 Last Name (required) c185ac05 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later b257d381 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) e5843ab4 Last Name (required) 482ccf1d Email (required) 9863e29b Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 7240536d Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Ca