    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/food-service-worker-manhattan-kansas-united-states-bf11611b-d8f3-4a25-9e40-9a265975f5a8": {
      "title": "Food Service Worker",
      "description": "Food Service Worker - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Food Service Worker - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Food Service Worker Apply Now Food Service Worker Food Service Workers make great food and service happen for K-State students. This benefits eligible position functions as part of a FUN cohesive team providing meals in a Residence Hall Dining facility. Early or late shifts available. 520724 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 21 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Food Service Workers are part of a team who make great food and service happen in a large residence hall dining center by providing quality food and service to fun and appreciative students and guests. The 40 hours per week work schedule offers a generous benefits package. The work schedule includes one Saturday or Sunday (one day) every other weekend. A day off will be scheduled either before or after the weekend day. Early and late shifts are available. Duties may include: • Preparing basic entrees and side dishes using standardized recipes and procedures. • Setting-up and preparing service platforms, salad bar, fruit/dessert area, and dining room areas for service of food. • Providing for customer needs during meal service. • Participating in daily meetings and effectively interacting with others. • Operating, cleaning, and sanitizing equipment in ware washing area and dish return belts. Cleaning and sanitizing all tableware trays, utensils, pots, pans. • Cleaning dining facility. • Laundering, folding, and storing linens. • May provide training and guidance to hourly student employees. About Us Housing and Dining Services is a large, complex, self-operated auxiliary department employing about 1,000 full and part-time staff. As a diverse group, we share the desire to provide exemplary services, products and facilities for our residents and other guests. The 2025 Princeton Review ranks us #2 Happiest Students, #2 Best Quality of Life, #8 Best College Residence Halls, and #14 Best Campus Food. What a great team to be part of! Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Preferred Qualifications: Some knowledge of large scale food preparation, equipment, health sanitation, and safety procedures. Ability to interact with others effectively, harmoniously, and in a courteous, pleasant manner. Ability to understand and follow written and oral instructions. Ability to learn to perform basic math computations; to accurately weigh and measure ingredients. Ability to use and care for equipment and handle food safely while preparing high quality products. Commitment to providing high quality services and products. Additional Role Information: Completion of Food Service Training within 6 months of employment. Work regularly requires moderate physical exertion to transport heavy items (up to 50 lbs.) repetitively. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the on-line application. Application Window Applications close on: October 21, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.00 per hour. Some work shifts may be eligible for an additional $.60 per hour shift differential. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 657ba263 Last Name (required) dc646cc6 Email (required) a8de50a8 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 4e6184fa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Dining / Hospitality Food Safety / Science / Systems Dining / Hospitality Food Safety / Science / Systems Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) f30acbdb Last Name (required) 64be081e Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 0c9f3d74 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) fe74882b Last Name (required) 11b88fd2 Email (required) 886cf168 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 442493e5 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 