    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/clinical-assistant-professor-equine-field-service-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor - Equine Field Service",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor - Equine Field Service - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Clinical Assistant Professor - Equine Field Service - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Clinical Assistant Professor - Equine Field Service Apply Now Clinical Assistant Professor - Equine Field Service The Department of Clinical Sciences, College of Veterinary Medicine, Kansas State University invites applications for a clinical assistant professor, term appointment, in Equine Field Service. Applicants must hold a DVM or equivalent degree. The successful candidate should be committed to academia and dedicated to contributing to a high-quality teaching program. Preference will be given to candidates with three years of clinical experience, internship training, or other advanced training appropriate for this position. 522315 Manhattan Clinical Sciences Academic / Faculty - 12 month Closing at: Nov 9 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Department of Clinical Sciences, College of Veterinary Medicine, Kansas State University invites applications for a clinical assistant professor, term appointment, in Equine Field Service. Applicants must hold a DVM or equivalent degree. The successful candidate should be committed to academia and dedicated to contributing to a high-quality teaching program. Preference will be given to candidates with three years of clinical experience, internship training, or other advanced training appropriate for this position. Directed clinical service activities include providing student oversight of field service patients, reproduction services, and patients with urgent care needs and minor surgeries. Collaboration with other services, faculty and house officers within the hospital is needed in this position. Work schedule will be flexible to meet service needs and provide occasional support of House Officers after hours. Teaching responsibilities include clinical, and possible didactic, instruction of veterinary students, clinical rounds, as well as participation in occasional outreach activities. The successful candidate must maintain a high-quality equine clinical service with a demonstrated commitment to building caseload and providing exceptional service and client communication. Salary will be commensurate with the applicant’s experience and qualifications. The start date is negotiable based on passing of a background check and submission of official transcripts. About Us The qualified person will join a dedicated team of equine medicine, surgery, field service, reproduction and large animal emergency medicine faculty members. In addition, each of the service areas have great support staff to fulfill the mission of quality patient care and exceptional customer service. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: DVM (or equivalent) degree The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: Three years of clinical experience, internship training, or other advanced training appropriate for this position Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: To apply, please complete the online application at http://www.k-state.edu/hcs/jobs/. Curriculum vitae, a letter of intent, and contact information for three professional references must be included. The letter of intent should describe the applicant’s strengths, professional goals, and vision for this position at Kansas State University. Inquiries may be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Laurie Beard at (785) 532-5700 or lbeard@vet.k-state.edu. Screening of applications will begin immediately and will close at 6 weeks after opening. Application Window Applications close: November 9, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Commensurate with experience and qualifications Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 5f34c0ee Last Name (required) 1cee4fb2 Email (required) 15b0d3bf Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 5b656ac5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 12 month Academic / Faculty - 12 month Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 84b5dfc3 Last Name (required) d4abe80c Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later f573f6f2 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 47e46672 Last Name (required) 8b789ad7 Email (required) 98a65584 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job d7ae2b6b Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to yo