    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/academic-advisor-salina-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Academic Advisor - Salina, Kansas, United States Academic Advisor - Salina, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Academic Advisor Apply Now Academic Advisor KSU Salina seeks an Academic Advisor to provide comprehensive academic advising and student success support for prospective, new, transfer, and continuing students. 522321 Salina, Kansas, United States Salina Enrollment Mgmt Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 18 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role KSU Salina seeks an Academic Advisor to provide comprehensive academic advising and student success support for prospective, new, transfer, and continuing students. This position assists students with academic planning, course selection, degree progress, and understanding university policies and requirements; evaluates academic records; connects students with university resources; and collaborates with faculty and staff to support student retention, persistence, and graduation. The Academic Advisor also contributes to orientation, enrollment, student success programming, and advising initiatives while maintaining accurate student records and providing proactive outreach to students in need of additional academic support. About Us K-State Salina Aerospace and Technology Campus is a distinctive part of Kansas State University. Located in Salina, Kansas, approximately 65 miles west of K-State's Manhattan campus, Salina offers a close-knit campus environment with the opportunities and resources of a Big 12 university. Our campus is centered on innovative learning, real-world experiences and industry connections. Students work alongside faculty and industry partners in fields that are shaping the future of aviation, engineering and technology. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. One year of relevant experience. Valid Driver's License required upon employment. The degree requirement ensures candidates possess the foundational knowledge in educational theory, student development and institutional policy interpretation essential to effective academic advising. These competencies are typically developed and rigorously validated only through the comprehensive curriculum and intensive experiential learning inherent in a formal degree program. Preferred Qualifications: Two years experience working in higher education Experience working in college admissions or academic advising Familiarity with K-State Salina academic programs and curriculum Master's degree in Counseling, Academic Advising, College Student Development, Education, or related field Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover Letter Resume Names and Contact Information for three current, professional references Application Window Applications close on: October 18, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $42,216 - $51,000, depending on qualifications Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 9381e8f7 Last Name (required) 03c78319 Email (required) b7a0dadc Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: f7a401e0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Advising / Support Administrative / Professional Academic Advising / Support Administrative / Professional Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Salina, Kansas, United States Salina, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) dee9c14c Last Name (required) e3daaa2d Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later cf434d3e Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) eb496413 Last Name (required) d51db6c5 Email (required) 036484fc Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 0510c3a0 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job’s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate’s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or s