    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/director-iii-info-technology-director-of-enterprise-systems-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Director III, Info Technology, Director of Enterprise Systems",
      "description": "Director III, Info Technology, Director of Enterprise Systems - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Director III, Info Technology, Director of Enterprise Systems - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Director III, Info Technology, Director of Enterprise Systems Apply Now Director III, Info Technology, Director of Enterprise Systems The Director of Enterprise Systems serves in a management level role, providing strategic and operational direction for the enterprise and administrative application systems. 522277 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Division of Info Tech Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Oct 21 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Director of Enterprise Systems serves in a management level role, providing strategic and operational direction for the enterprise and administrative application systems. The director will work closely with institutional leadership, senior IT leadership, and representatives of administrative and academic departments to develop and execute the institution’s administrative technology tactical plans. The position provides analysis and recommendations to improve and expand applications, system integrations, and application performance. This position is responsible for the management and implementation of the institution’s ERP (Finance, HR, and Student) systems, CRM, facilities, parking, and other administrative systems. This includes supervision, ongoing training, monitoring system effectiveness, and evaluation for staff supporting these systems. Communication across organizational units within IT, managers, and functional administrators is essential in support of administrative technology planning. About Us Kansas State University's Division of Information Technology is committed to providing excellent IT services to the K-State community in support of the teaching, learning, research, and service missions. We offer a wide range of information, technology, and communications services. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and ten years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and five to ten years of experience in higher education enterprise application development, implementation and support. Master’s degree from an accredited institution in computer science, information systems, business administration or related field Demonstrated ability to lead a team and effective interpersonal communication skills Demonstrated project management skills, including the ability to effectively deploy resources and manage multiple projects of diverse scopes Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty High level of energy, enthusiasm, and ability to be innovative and creative Effective verbal and written communication skills Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills Detail and results-oriented Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: October 21, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $95,903-$127,072 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 07ed06a6 Last Name (required) 83c59da4 Email (required) 777b6df7 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 33ac3f3b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Computer Science / Information Technology Computer Science / Information Technology Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) fb51bf04 Last Name (required) cd63aa4c Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later af7ae699 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) e2f747a5 Last Name (required) 1d8b83e8 Email (required) dbf1dab1 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 2082ee3c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop 