    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/fellow-post-doc-manhattan-kansas-united-states-4f9d750a-4281-4171-915d-3a4c45a73061": {
      "title": "Fellow (Post Doc)",
      "description": "Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Fellow (Post Doc) Apply Now Fellow (Post Doc) The Yang Laboratory at Kansas State University is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Fellow to conduct interdisciplinary research at the interface of biomedical science, biomaterials, food-as-medicine, and precision health. The successful candidate will contribute to projects investigating how engineered biomaterials, bioactive compounds, nutrients, and delivery systems interact with biological systems to modulate health and disease. Research will integrate in vivo animal models, mammalian cell culture, and organoid-based models with molecular and cellular analyses. The postdoctoral fellow will have opportunities to develop independent research directions, publish high-impact research, participate in interdisciplinary collaborations, mentor undergraduate and graduate researchers, and contribute to preparation of manuscripts, presentations, and research proposals. 522309 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Grain and Food Science Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 13 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Yang Laboratory at Kansas State University is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Fellow to conduct interdisciplinary research at the interface of biomedical science, biomaterials, food-as-medicine, and precision health. The successful candidate will contribute to projects investigating how engineered biomaterials, bioactive compounds, nutrients, and delivery systems interact with biological systems to modulate health and disease. Research will integrate in vivo animal models, mammalian cell culture, and organoid-based models with molecular and cellular analyses. The postdoctoral fellow will have opportunities to develop independent research directions, publish high-impact research, participate in interdisciplinary collaborations, mentor undergraduate and graduate researchers, and contribute to preparation of manuscripts, presentations, and research proposals. About Us The Department of Grain and Food Science is committed to providing high-quality education, advancing innovation in grain and food science research, and building strong industry partnerships to meet the evolving needs of global food systems. Our faculty includes several current and former Grain and Food Science members who are ranked among the world’s top 2% of researchers in a 2020 Stanford University study. For more than 110 years, Kansas State University has been a global leader in flour milling and industry-focused education. Since 1951, it has remained one of the few institutions worldwide to offer four-year bachelor’s degrees in Bakery Science and Management, Feed and Pet Food Science, Food Science, and Milling Science and Management. Our internationally recognized graduate program also provides a wide range of opportunities for both applied and fundamental research, leading to master’s and doctoral degrees in grain science, food science, and related fields. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: • Ph.D. or equivalent doctoral degree in biomedical sciences, molecular and cellular biology, pharmacology, immunology, physiology, bioengineering, biotechnology, microbiology, nutritional sciences, or a closely related discipline. The degree requirement is necessary to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: • Extensive hands-on experience with mouse models and in vivo experimental procedures. • Experience developing or working with organoids, intestinal organoids, primary cells, 3D cell culture, or advanced in vitro models. • Experience with gastrointestinal biology, immunology, inflammation, metabolic disease, nutrition, microbiome research, or related biomedical areas. • Experience with flow cytometry or fluorescence-activated cell sorting (FACS). • Experience with histology, immunohistochemistry, immunofluorescence, or confocal microscopy. • Experience with qPCR, Western blotting, ELISA, RNA sequencing, single-cell analysis, or other molecular profiling techniques. Sponsorship eligibility: This position is eligible for sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. KSU online Page Up application 2. Resume 3. Letter of Interest 4. List of three references with email address and phone number listed Application Window Applications close on:10/13/2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $47,476 - $65,000 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 01478603 Last Name (required) bd6912fd Email (required) 6b953d56 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 96ded332 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture Animal Sciences / Livestock Medical Natural / Quantitative Sciences Research / Scientific / Grants Agriculture Animal Sciences / Livestock Medical Natural / Quantitative Sciences Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 534b64fc Las