    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/accountant-i-manhattan-kansas-united-states-42375aa2-0f80-41ac-9257-0a22154f0740": {
      "title": "Accountant I",
      "description": "Accountant I - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Accountant I - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Accountant I Apply Now Accountant I Accountant I to perform accounting functions including accounts receivable/payable, reconciliations, budgeting, payments, financial reporting, and program accounting while supporting accurate, timely financial operations. 522308 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 21 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Department of Housing and Dining Services (HDS) seeks qualified applicants for an Accountant I to join our financial operations team. This full-time position offers the opportunity to collaborate with others and participate in accounting work critical to the success of a large, complex, self-operated department. HDS is a $50M operation serving more than 4,500 residents. Duties and responsibilities include: • Manage and track $2.0M non-student accounts receivable process, from invoicing through payment and reconciliation. • Process and reconcile accounts payable for key revenue generating areas and process interdepartmental transactions. • Monitor outstanding balances and assist with collection efforts. • Reconcile revenues, expenses, and account balances across multiple systems. • Prepare journal entries, reports, and financial records. • Support budgets and purchasing for student and educational programs. • Process Dining Dollar redemptions and related vendor payments. • Process Foundation payments, reimbursements, scholarships, and awards. • Maintain accurate electronic financial records and documentation. • Work with university staff, students, vendors, and external organizations. • Learn and apply university and state financial policies and procedures. About Us The Department of Housing and Dining Services offers award-winning dining centers, residence halls, and apartment neighborhoods. We pride ourselves in taking excellent care of our residents, and that is reflected in our recent Princeton Review rankings. The 2025 Princeton Review ranks us #2 Happiest Students, #2 Best Quality of Life, #8 Best College Residence Halls, and #14 Best Campus Food. Functional areas within the department include administrative, maintenance, student living, and dining services. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and one year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in business, accounting, finance or related field Two years accounting/auditing experience or minimum three years in an accounting role requiring familiarity with university, state or federal accounting compliance and GAAP principles, including revenue accrual and reconciliation procedures. Cash handling experience, including auditing cash funds in a retail environment. Experience with PeopleSoft, Oracle, Sap or other similar large ERP financial system. Familiarity with document imaging systems and records retention policies. Ability to interact and communicate effectively with others, including giving direction to student staff and student organization officers. Ability to communicate tactfully when contacting receivables customers with outstanding balances. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Online application Resume Names and contact information for three professional references Letter of interest Application Window Applications close on: October 21, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $17.00 - $19.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) a9ff8a62 Last Name (required) e2385656 Email (required) 33a1c419 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 80ede0a7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Business / Accounting / Finance Dining / Hospitality Administrative / Professional Business / Accounting / Finance Dining / Hospitality Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 74828c77 Last Name (required) d6813bad Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 2987cc11 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 1121b99a Last Name (required) 40bc1895 Email (required) c966a62e Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 7174af0c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captio