      "title": "Fellow (Post Doc)",
      "description": "Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Fellow (Post Doc) Apply Now Fellow (Post Doc) This position is focused on conducting research but may include formal instructional responsibilities. The role includes mentored training for the purpose of further increasing research expertise in a specialized area in order to pursue a specific career path. 522230 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Biology Staff Part Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 15 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position is focused on conducting research but may include formal instructional responsibilities. The role includes mentored training for the purpose of further increasing research expertise in a specialized area in order to pursue a specific career path. About Us The Division of Biology at Kansas State University is composed of a dynamic group of tenure-track, research, and instructional faculty, as well as a large number of postdoctoral research associates, graduate students, and support staff. All of these individuals are essential to accomplish the Division of Biology’s mission, to generate and disseminate high-quality biological scientific knowledge through teaching, research, service, and outreach. The research, teaching, and service interests of these individuals, spanning all areas of biological research, teaching and training at the postdoctoral, graduate, and undergraduate levels, as well as service and outreach contributions to the broader scientific community and the public. Worksite Description This position is On-site . N/A All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: PhD. The degree requirement is necessary to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Valid driver's license. Professional experience working with data and statistical analysis Professional experience working with agencies on applied quantitative problems Statistical experience with an array of quantitative procedures (general and generalized linear model procedures, multivariate analyses, machine learning, specialized visualizations) Knowledge of fish ecology theory, fisheries methods, conservation practice Experience communicating with state and federal decisionmakers Demonstrated knowledge of AI large language models Peer reviewed publications Preferred Qualifications: PhD > 5 years professional experience working with data and statistical analysis > 5 years experience working with agencies on applied quantitative problems Extensive statistical experience with an array of quantitative procedures (general and generalized linear model procedures, multivariate analyses, machine learning, specialized visualizations) Knowledge of fish ecology theory, fisheries methods, conservation practice Extensive experience communicating with state and federal decisionmakers Demonstrated knowledge of AI large language models Substantial record of peer reviewed publications (> 20) Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Contact information for three references Application Window Applications close on:October 15, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $41,995.20 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) ade52a56 Last Name (required) 1726d675 Email (required) 20e60528 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 117e3b3c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown 