      "title": "Mail Specialist",
      "description": "Mail Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Mail Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Mail Specialist Apply Now Mail Specialist This position exists to provide mail service to the campus community by sorting, delivering, and collecting all campus and federal mail from various campus locations. This position will process all outgoing mail using various carriers (USPS, FedEx, UPS, and DHL) while conforming to Domestic and International regulations by utilizing shipping software, handheld scanners, and various computer programs. 522312 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fac Postal Center Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 30 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position exists to provide mail service to the campus community by sorting, delivering, and collecting all campus and federal mail from various campus locations. This position will process all outgoing mail using various carriers (USPS, FedEx, UPS, and DHL) while conforming to Domestic and International regulations by utilizing shipping software, handheld scanners, and various computer programs. About Us This position exists to provide mail service to the campus community by sorting, delivering, and collecting campus and federal mail from various campus locations. Worksite Description This position is On-site . Employee in this position is allowed considerable latitude in completing all work assignments. Instructions are given verbally and in writing. United States Postal Service manuals, United Parcel Service manuals, charts, and bulletins are provided and updated regularly. Assignments are given verbally and in writing. Very particular attention is given to detail. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and one year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: Prefer high school graduate or equivalent and two years’ experience in a major mail room operation. Prefer knowledge of United States Postal Service and United Parcel Service regulations, rapid reading ability and memorization skills for sorting of mail, and data entry ability. Additional Role Information: This position exists to provide mail service to the campus community by sorting, delivering, and collecting campus and federal mail from various campus locations. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover Letter Resume (3) Professional References Application Window Applications close on: 10-30-2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Hourly $ 13.22 - 19.82 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 1c0dc314 Last Name (required) c6be526d Email (required) e59393c0 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 25e2bc23 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Administrative / Professional Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) c21cd7de 