    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/hvac-technician-manhattan-kansas-united-states-db1ea73d-f45a-4456-b405-df343ba9a2cd": {
      "title": "HVAC Technician",
      "description": "HVAC Technician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States HVAC Technician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode HVAC Technician Apply Now HVAC Technician This position exists to provide highly skilled HVAC services to the campus community to allow for personal comfort in the various buildings at KSU at the advanced/master level. Must participate in mandatory on-call program, in which 24 hour emergency availability is required. 522306 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fac Building Maintenance Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 14 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position exists to provide highly skilled HVAC services to the campus community to allow for personal comfort in the various buildings at KSU at the advanced/master level. Must participate in mandatory on-call program, in which 24 hour emergency availability is required. About Us The Division of Facilities' maintenance personnel conduct routine maintenance on building systems and equipment to ensure the operational reliability of our campus' building systems. This maintenance involves regular, scheduled service to maintain equipment functionality without the need for immediate repairs. Many of the older buildings have systems and equipment that have exceeded their expected lifespan, highlighting the value of a strong preventive maintenance program. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Two years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Valid Drivers License Preferred Qualifications: Two years of experience in refrigeration-air/conditioning repair work. Four years of experience in refrigeration and air conditioning work including two at the journey level. Journey level experience in electronic control service and repair. Journey level experience in heating systems including electric, gas fired, heat pump, steam, and hot water. Additional Role Information: Have and maintain a valid driver’s license. Valid EPA Refrigerant Recovery Certificate with a universal rating. Medical certification for respirator use within probationary period. Maintain medical certification for respirator annually. Daily: All types of HVAC equipment, state vehicles, EMS computer software, Electrical meters, AIMS computer software, electrical safety equipment, oxygen-acetylene torches, vacuum pumps, refrigerant recovery equipment, and refrigeration gauges. Subject to on-call, standby and inclement weather response. This position is essential. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Application Application Window Applications close on: October 14, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $20.30 - $ 31.45 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 2aa9ed1c Last Name (required) cb45b4d3 Email (required) 213ab0a4 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 2caaa76b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (r