    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/veterinary-assistant-large-animal-manhattan-kansas-united-states-aca32929-a591-4cf5-8ebd-815e01951066": {
      "title": "Veterinary Assistant – Large Animal",
      "description": "Veterinary Assistant – Large Animal - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Assistant – Large Animal - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Veterinary Assistant – Large Animal Apply Now Veterinary Assistant – Large Animal The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking a Veterinary Assistant to join our dedicated team to help facilitate exemplary patient care and quality customer service. This position is responsible for providing technical assistance services to the KSU-VHC in equine, livestock and equine field service. They will coordinate technical services for veterinary care to client, teaching and research patients presented to the equine, livestock services and field service department(s). This position is also responsible for monitoring 4th year veterinary students and entering information into the electronic medical records system. Stocking and cleanliness of the large animal barn as deemed necessary. Lastly, this position is responsible for coordination of animal treatments and diagnostics along with the supervising DVM on the case. Working hours for this position will be Thursday-Saturday, 8am-8pm. 522293 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Health Center Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 14 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking a Veterinary Assistant to join our dedicated team to help facilitate exemplary patient care and quality customer service. This position is responsible for providing technical assistance services to the KSU-VHC in equine, livestock and equine field service. They will coordinate technical services for veterinary care to client, teaching and research patients presented to the equine, livestock services and field service department(s). This position is also responsible for monitoring 4th year veterinary students and entering information into the electronic medical records system. Stocking and cleanliness of the large animal barn as deemed necessary. Lastly, this position is responsible for coordination of animal treatments and diagnostics along with the supervising DVM on the case. Working hours for this position will be Thursday-Saturday, 8am-8pm. About Us The Veterinary Health Center is a teaching hospital that offers routine, emergency, and specialty care services. The VHC strives to provide exceptional care for patients from high-quality routine healthcare to state-of-the-art advanced therapy for seriously ill patients. The Veterinary Health Center is located in Manhattan, Kansas which is a vibrant college community with a population of over 55,000 in the Flint Hills. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes 24 vacation days plus other paid time off (holidays, sick, and discretionary), health insurance, life insurance, and retirement plans. To see what benefits are available, please visit: www.ksvhc.org/about/employment/recruitment.html Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) One year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: 1 year of relevant large animal handling and hospital setting experience. Ability to work with and provide preventative maintenance for ordinary medical equipment. Ability to handle, restrain, and provide medical treatments to domestic animals. Willingness to master new techniques. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter 3. Contact information for three professional references Application Window Applications close: October 14, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.50 - $16.50 hr Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 90804d33 Last Name (required) ad93db2a Email (required) 0dd6a6d8 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 32cb043b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 24378021 Last Name (required) 000e948b Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 6e2e5c2e Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) bd6f2dae Last Name (required) cea6dbd7 Email (required) bc82bc0f Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job ba33f1dc Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters D