    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/maintenance-and-repair-tech-ii-manhattan-kansas-united-states-ba7449a2-3e35-4fa3-8ef4-a83330c6b524": {
      "title": "Maintenance and Repair Tech II",
      "description": "Maintenance and Repair Tech II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Maintenance and Repair Tech II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Maintenance and Repair Tech II Apply Now Maintenance and Repair Tech II This position exists to perform maintenance to utilities, roads, sidewalks, curbs, lights, parking lots, signs, street sweeping, and snow removal. 522299 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fac Power Plant & Utilities Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 13 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position exists to perform maintenance to utilities, roads, sidewalks, curbs, lights, parking lots, signs, street sweeping, and snow removal. About Us The Utilities department oversees all utility infrastructure, including electrical, natural gas, water, sanitary sewer, and storm sewer. Furthermore, they manage roads, parking lots, sidewalks, and all outdoor lighting as well as generators. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: One year of relevant experience. Various training and/or certification may be required. Valid driver's license Preferred Qualifications: High school graduate or equivalent is preferred. At least two years electrical, carpentry, and/or plumbing experience is preferred. Equipment operation to include fork lifts, skid steers, and front end loaders is preferred Ability to listen and work with detailed direction. Additional Role Information: Have and maintain a valid driver’s license. Must have the mobility to access small work areas (i.e., air handling units), climb ladders, and work in varying temperatures and heights. Work involves considerable physical exertion to transport equipment/supplies weighing 50 pounds or more, unassisted, regularly, on a daily basis. Daily: Hand tools, hand-operated electric tools, Socket sets, open-end wrenches, torque wrenches, current/circuit tracers, ohm/amp meters, grease guns, oil cans, ladders, state vehicles, computers. As required: Genie let, scissor left, JLG lift, Upright boom lift. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Application Application Window Applications close on: October 13, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $17.00 hourly Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 370fcb01 Last Name (required) 42b6c109 Email (required) 996de644 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 18ed1d45 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) dcefa6e4 Last Name (required) 96809596 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 641782bc Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 41e6b1a3 Last Name (required) aa834baf Email (required) 96f1c5ef Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 635d75fd Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivab