    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/agricultural-tech-ii-research-colby-kansas-united-states-aa8619f8-481d-4a2f-8a03-4b7c40074b9b": {
      "title": "Agricultural Tech II Research",
      "description": "Agricultural Tech II Research - Colby, Kansas, United States Agricultural Tech II Research - Colby, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Agricultural Tech II Research Apply Now Agricultural Tech II Research This position, which is under the supervision of the Cropping Systems Agronomist, provides assistance to the research crop scientists and crop research team. The worker assists the supervisor in establishing, maintaining, and collecting research data and harvesting field and greenhouse research plots. Following established procedures, the worker provides assistance in data entry and analysis. Provides assistance maintaining lab, greenhouse, and field equipment. 521917 Colby, Kansas NW Research Ext Center Colby Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Nov 30 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position, which is under the supervision of the Cropping Systems Agronomist, provides assistance to the research crop scientists and crop research team. The worker assists the supervisor in establishing, maintaining, and collecting research data and harvesting field and greenhouse research plots. Following established procedures, the worker provides assistance in data entry and analysis. Provides assistance maintaining lab, greenhouse, and field equipment. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires at least 1-year of relevant experience in agricultural sciences. Must be 18 years old in order to operate & maintenance general farm equipment including but not limited to tractor, sprayer, combine, mower as well as a soil water instrument which contains radioactive material as required by the KSU Radiation Safety Office. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: Education in the biological sciences, agricultural sciences, agricultural systems, or agriculture mechanics. Knowledge of how to operate & maintenance general farm equipment as stated in required experience Knowledge of the hazards and effects of pesticides (herbicides, insecticides, fungicides, etc.) and the ability to read and interpret labels and MSDS/SDS instructions regarding safe and proper use of agricultural chemicals. Skill and ability to use computers and software, such as MS word, spreadsheet and electronic data transfer. Willingness to communicate errors or problems. Ability to read and follow spoken and written plans. Additional Role Information: Valid driver's license, upon employment, in order to drive state-owned vehicles. Work requires physical exertion and exposure to inclement weather. Must be able to transport in excess of 50 lbs., not exceeding 100 lbs. unassisted on a regular basis. Equipment used includes field scientific instruments, lab instruments, computers and grain processing facilities. The position involves regular (daily) use or contact with motorized vehicles such as pickup trucks and utility vehicles. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Three professional references Cover letter (optional) Relevant licenses and certifications (optional) Application Window Applications close on: November 30, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $16.76 - $26.84/hr Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 06abaa11 Last Name (required) f007604c Email (required) a5cc259b Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: b156d4d1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture Agronomy Plant Sciences Research / Scientific / Grants Agriculture Agronomy Plant Sciences Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Colby, Kansas, United States Colby, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 1d7d057c Last Name (required) 5788293a Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 0317a741 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 05331385 Last Name (required) 181aa519 Email (required) 76494327 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 6739683c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization: Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid Work Options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating you can visit the site apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State’s background check policy . Interview Preference: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page. Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) b7b13a38 Last Name (required) 57ade829 Email (required) ebe0512b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) bcc71192 Last Name (required) 389ff9ce Email (required) e8b90607 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"
