    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/custodial-specialist-jardine-apts-manhattan-kansas-united-states-f7982d6d-04af-41f8-b620-b99384eac31d": {
      "title": "Custodial Specialist (Jardine Apts.)",
      "description": "Custodial Specialist (Jardine Apts.) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Custodial Specialist (Jardine Apts.) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Custodial Specialist (Jardine Apts.) Apply Now Custodial Specialist (Jardine Apts.) Housing and Dining Services takes pride in taking excellent care of our residents and guests, You can be part of a team that provides services to Jardine Apartments. The team ensures that facilities are clean, sanitized, tidy, and welcoming for residents and guests. 521568 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 16 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Join a cleaning team that provides services to Jardine Apartments , an on-campus community offering more than 800 apartments. The team provides inviting spaces to students, faculty, staff and guests by ensuring that facilities are clean, sanitized, tidy, safe, and welcoming for residents and guests. Regular work hours are 7:30 a.m.–4:00 p.m., Monday–Friday. Duties include: • Performs heavy industrial “ceiling to floor” cleaning in vacant apartments, administrative areas, and classrooms. • Maintains attractive surroundings by picking up litter and debris, cleaning outdoor stairwells, handrails, landings, sidewalks and commons areas. Removes snow, spreads salt and sand stairs and sidewalks. • Provides hotel type housekeeping services for conference groups and other guests staying in departmental facilities. • Makes minor repairs to equipment and stores equipment securely and properly. About Us Housing and Dining Services is a large, self-operated auxiliary department serving more than 5,000 students that call the K-State campus home. This \"home away from home\" meets more than the basic needs of students living with us — we provide affordable, safe and engaging accommodations and services for our residents, while finding unique ways to support them in their academic pursuits. You can help make our residents and visitors feel welcome and comfortable! Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: No minimum requirements Various training and/or certification may be required Valid driver's license Preferred Qualifications: Custodial experience and knowledge of commercial/industrial cleaning equipment. Ability to work harmoniously and effectively with others and to communicate effectively both orally and in writing. Knowledge of tools, equipment and materials used in custodial work and their use of application. Ability to make basic repairs, perform basic maintenance tasks. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: On-line application Application Window Applications close on: October 16, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 26a68dd7 Last Name (required) 77b0edc6 Email (required) 2b1cd790 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: bcd8155d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this