    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/developer-ii-erp-systems-developer-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Developer II, ERP Systems Developer",
      "description": "Developer II, ERP Systems Developer - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Developer II, ERP Systems Developer - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Developer II, ERP Systems Developer Apply Now Developer II, ERP Systems Developer The PeopleSoft Developer II – Data, Reporting & Integrations provides technical development and support for the PeopleSoft CS and HCM environments, with primary responsibility for ERP data flows, reporting solutions, and system integrations. This position designs, develops, and supports secure, reliable, and scalable ERP data exchanges and reporting capabilities that enable institutional decision-making and cross-system interoperability. This role works collaboratively with functional analysts, data operations, business intelligence teams, and integration partners to ensure accurate, timely, and secure information exchange across university systems. 522242 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Division of Info Tech Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 30 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The PeopleSoft Developer II – Data, Reporting & Integrations provides technical development and support for the PeopleSoft CS and HCM environments, with primary responsibility for ERP data flows, reporting solutions, and system integrations. This position designs, develops, and supports secure, reliable, and scalable ERP data exchanges and reporting capabilities that enable institutional decision-making and cross-system interoperability. This role works collaboratively with functional analysts, data operations, business intelligence teams, and integration partners to ensure accurate, timely, and secure information exchange across university systems. About Us Enterprise Systems leads strategies to ensure technologies are used efficiently and cost-effectively while leveraging stakeholders' feedback to guide improvements and adjustments. Ensures technology decisions align with the University goals; system infrastructure is functional and efficient, builds data protection processes, and monitors key performance indicators (KPIs). Manages day-to-day technology and client service operations to improve infrastructure costs, performance, and user satisfaction. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma (or equivalent) and six years of relevant experience demonstrating proficiency in at least one object-oriented or procedural programming language such as Java, C#, or Python; working knowledge of SQL and relational database concepts; basic understanding of web technologies including HTML and JavaScript; and the ability to read and interpret data models, entity relationship diagrams (ERDs), and system diagrams. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: • Bachelor's degree preferably in technical or business-related discipline. • Excellent oral and written communication skills. • Five or more years of relevant experience supporting PeopleSoft CS and/or HCM environments. • Experience designing and supporting ETL processes and enterprise reporting. • Knowledge of data governance, security best practices, and structured data modeling. • Ability to translate business requirements into technical data and integration solutions. • Strong analytical and troubleshooting skills. • Strong written and verbal communication skills with a high attention to detail. • PeopleTools: Application Designer, Application Engine, PeopleCode, Application Packages, SQR. • Familiarity with PUM images and update processes. • Fluid, Work Centers, Activity Guides, AWE, Data over DMS. • PeopleSoft security / Unix / AppStream. • Higher-ed environment experience. • Understanding of Oracle PeopleSoft CS and/or HCM functional processes. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 30, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $70,000-$85,000 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) bf2546f6 Last Name (required) 6ca94ec8 Email (required) c54bfcf6 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: f4eca157 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Computer Science / Information Technology Computer Science / Information Technology Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 0ca5956c Last Name (required) 5308d9ca Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 69d0ed3e Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) e150139f Last Name (required) 51768c26 Email (required) 47934966 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 81608f09 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currentl