    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/director-i-information-tech-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Director I, Information Tech",
      "description": "Director I, Information Tech - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Director I, Information Tech - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Director I, Information Tech Apply Now Director I, Information Tech Kansas State University seeks an IT Director for the College of Business Administration to lead the implementation of strategic information technology plans. The director provides leadership for all college technical systems, data systems and college departmental applications and may manage and mentor IT personnel resources (including full-time IT staff or technicians and part-time hourly or graduate student resources). 522274 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Business Administration Dean Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Oct 21 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The IT Director in the College of Business Administration develops and directs the implementation of strategic information technology plans. The director provides leadership for all college technical systems, data systems and college departmental applications and may manage and mentor IT personnel resources (including full-time IT staff or technicians and part-time hourly or graduate student resources). This position is responsible for ensuring the college's technical operations and security posture are aligned and comply with IT policies, procedures and standards set forth by the state, university and the college (if applicable). The incumbent is responsible for providing IT leadership and oversight within the college and associated units and supports college strategic plans through a future-forward approach to technology resources. This position typically provides direct management of IT services. The IT Director will report directly to the AVP for Academic IT and Research which is positioned within central IT along with a dotted reporting line to the Dean of the College of Business Administration. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and ten years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in computer science, information technology or related field. Experience in technology troubleshooting, assisting, and training. Experience administering servers in small to medium sized server environments. Experience managing IT staff members responsible for providing front-line support for hardware and departmental IT systems. Experience conducting and directing research into IT issues and products. Experience working in a higher education environment. Experience building business case scenarios and working with technology allocation and budgets. Extensive experience working in a team-oriented, collaborative environment. Strong leadership skills Excellent written and oral communication skills. Excellent interpersonal skills Ability to present ideas in business-friendly and user-friendly language. Highly self-motivated and directed Keen attention to detail Proven analytical, evaluative and problem-solving abilities. Ability to effectively prioritize and execute tasks in a high-pressure environment. Exceptional customer service orientation. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: October 21, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $70,835-$104,500 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) b607b3a8 Last Name (required) 5120034f Email (required) 982db616 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 25affb80 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Business / Accounting / Finance Computer Science / Information Technology Business / Accounting / Finance Computer Science / Information Technology Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 4a1976ce Last Name (required) c8bc2162 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later bb798d62 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 1d85171c Last Name (required) 2a1bee7f Email (required) e503ed4c Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job a77447a5 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Mage