    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/asst-director-and-career-engagement-consultant-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Asst Director and Career Engagement Consultant",
      "description": "Asst Director and Career Engagement Consultant - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Asst Director and Career Engagement Consultant - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Asst Director and Career Engagement Consultant Apply Now Asst Director and Career Engagement Consultant The Assistant Director will serve as a dedication Career Engagement Consultant for the College of Engineering. This position integrates career education directly into the academic experience to promote transformative career development across the student lifecycle. 522278 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Career Center Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Oct 16 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Assistant Director will serve as a dedication Career Engagement Consultant for the College of Engineering. This position integrates career education directly into the academic experience to promote transformative career development across the student lifecycle. As a leader within the university’s career success ecosystem, the Assistant Director empowers students through curriculum integration, robust industry partnerships, and technology-driven solutions. This role moves away from high-volume transactional advising to focus on architecting a unified student journey that connects academic planning, work-integrated learning, and clear career outcomes upholding K-State’s R1 public land-grant mission. About Us The Career Center facilitates the career readiness of all students throughout the K-State community. The Career Center offers job search training, career advising, employer connections, and a staff dedicated to assisting students in the career development process. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and seven years of relevant experience in higher education, program management, or curriculum development. Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Preferred Qualifications: • Master’s degree in Counseling, Higher Education Administration, Student Affairs, or a related field. • Experience in curriculum design, learning outcome assessment, and evidence-based decision making. • Experience supervising staff or directing the work of student employees. • Educational background in/knowledge of Engineering. • Knowledge of and experience applying career development theory and NACE career competencies. • Proficiency in career management platforms (Handshake) and learning management systems (Canvas). Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Letter of interest (documents may be addressed to Tiffany Coetzee, Career Consultant 2. Resume 3. Names, emails and phone numbers of three professional references Application Window Applications close on:Oct 16, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $22.38-$29.11 hourly Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) a64fae34 Last Name (required) 31bf6751 Email (required) 270982f8 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: dc11c9fb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Advising / Support Executive / Director / Management Student Affairs / Services Academic Advising / Support Executive / Director / Management Student Affairs / Services Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 6221816e Last Name (required) 82bdeca2 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 07d303d2 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) cde90c0b Last Name (required) da19cb2d Email (required) 36767bdb Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 8ed417d7 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Mon