    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/associate-director-of-extension-programs-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Extension Programs",
      "description": "Associate Director of Extension Programs - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Associate Director of Extension Programs - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Associate Director of Extension Programs Apply Now Associate Director of Extension Programs The Associate Director of Extension Programs provides strategic, programmatic, fiscal, and organizational leadership for K-State Extension, advancing statewide priorities, aligning resources with goals, and expanding Extension’s impact across Kansas communities. 522270 Manhattan Extension Programs Academic / Faculty - 12 month Closing at: Oct 21 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Associate Director of Extension Programs serves as a senior faculty leader within K-State Extension, providing strategic, programmatic, fiscal, and organizational leadership for Extension’s statewide educational mission. Reporting directly to the Assistant Vice President – Director for Extension, this position leads the development and implementation of strategic priorities, ensures alignment of programs and resources with organizational goals, and advances Extension’s impact across Kansas communities. The role provides oversight for Extension’s statewide program portfolio, including agriculture and natural resources, family and consumer sciences, community vitality, youth development, and emerging program areas. The position oversees assigned budgets and resources, ensuring responsible stewardship of public and external funds and data-informed decision-making. The Associate Director serves as a systems-level leader responsible for advancing the relevance, quality, impact, and long-term sustainability of Extension programming across Kansas. The position identifies emerging statewide needs; develops cross-program and transdisciplinary priorities; leads strategic and grant-funded initiatives; builds accountability and evaluation structures; and cultivates partnerships with federal agencies, foundations, industry, community organizations, and university collaborators, and resources necessary for Extension to address complex community and statewide challenges. The position also serves as a senior representative of K-State Extension, strengthening relationships with stakeholders, policymakers, educational partners, and Cooperative Extension systems nationwide. The Associate Director works closely with Extension administration, program leaders, faculty, specialists, educators, academic and administrative partners, state and federal agencies, community organizations, and external stakeholders to ensure Extension programming remains research-based, responsive, outcomes-focused, and aligned with Kansas State University’s land-grant mission. This is a 1.0 FTE, tenure or non-tenure faculty appointment. About Us K-State Extension improves Kansans' lives, livelihoods and communities through education, research, engagement and leadership. With scientists, educators and volunteers in each of the state's 105 counties, our professionals strive to make the university's research and scientific accomplishments accessible and relevant to every household. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Earned Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree. Demonstrated leadership and supervisory experience in a complex organization. Proven ability to translate strategic vision into actionable plans and measurable outcomes. Experience in strategic planning, program development, evaluation, budget management, and fiscal accountability. Demonstrated strong written, verbal, interpersonal, and stakeholder communication skills Understanding of Extension audiences, communities, and needs served by Extension and commitment to research-based educational programming that addresses the needs of Kansas communities. Ability and willingness to travel throughout Kansas and nationally as needed, including occasional evening and weekend commitments. Valid driver’s license. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: Five or more years of professional Cooperative Extension experience with increasing leadership responsibility. Experience designing and delivering Extension, outreach, or community-based educational programming. Demonstrated success in acquiring, administering, and managing external funding from federal, state, multistate initiatives, foundation, philanthropic, or partnership sources. Experience developing and leading interdisciplinary teams and fostering cultures of collaboration, innovation, accountability, and continuous improvement. Knowledge of transdisciplinary approaches to addressing statewide and community challenges. Experience using technology and digital tools to enhance educational delivery, accessibility, and stakeholder engagement. Experience working with legislators, government agencies, industry representatives, community organizations, and external partners. Additional Role Information: Knowledge, Skills, and Competencies The successful candidate will demonstrate strategic leadership, organizational awareness, and the ability to balance long-term vision with operational execution. Strong supervisory, coaching, team-building, decision-making, and relationship-management skills are essential, along with the ability to influence and collaborate across organizational boundaries. The position requires expertise in program quality, evaluation, resource stewardship, accountability, and continuous improvement, as well as a strong commitment to the land-grant mission and public service. Scope and Impact This position influences Extension programming and services across Kansas, shaping statewide priorities, resource allocation, organizational partnerships, externally funded initiatives, and program effectiveness. The role requires independent judgment, strategic decision-making, and the ability to align diverse stakeholders around common goals while advancing Extension’s mission, visibility, and long-term impact. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover letter CV/Resume Three professional references Application Window Applications close on: October 21, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Salary commensurate with education and experience. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) c7b44d14 Last Name (required) c412aa1c Email (required) 76cccf8e Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 59edbba5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Executive / Director / Management Extension Agent / Educator Executive / Director / Management Extension Agent / Educator Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 12 month Academic / Faculty - 12 month Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 71f27a26 Last Name (required) 0db5c758 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 8447600d Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) e45f5077 Last Name (required) 27a9d978 Email (required) 1dcc61e1 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job b275c17e Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job’s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate’s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State’s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 988b3211 Last Name (required) f288df88 Email (required) 649a6a73 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 