    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/program-project-coordinator-manhattan-kansas-united-states-dcd70c51-92d5-4f49-95d8-10739bd8197f": {
      "title": "Program/Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Program/Project Coordinator - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Program/Project Coordinator - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Program/Project Coordinator Apply Now Program/Project Coordinator The Student & Academic Services Office seeks a Project Coordinator to support the Associate Dean and manage course scheduling, scholarships, international programs, and other strategic projects, ensuring efficient operations and adapting to evolving college needs. 522250 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Arch Planning & Design Dean of Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Oct 18 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Project Coordinator provides executive support to the Associate Dean and is responsible for managing projects and activities related to Course Scheduling, Scholarship Awards, International Programs, and other projects as determined by the Associate Dean. The responsibilities of the Project Coordinator are expected to be complex and varied and will respond to the evolving needs of the programs and the College of Architecture, Planning and Design. About Us The College of Architecture, Planning and Design (APDesign) consists of students, faculty and alumni across all disciplines, united by a shared passion for design. We offer a variety of programs in the architecture, community development, design and planning fields. Our programs teach students to collaborate with their peers, constantly try new approaches to problems and redefine the traditional boundaries of design. Our faculty and students are leaders and award-winners, representing APDesign and K-State across the nation. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and four years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Preferred Qualifications: Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to work on complex, multifaceted projects. Ability to make independent decisions, multi-task, prioritize, and meet deadlines. Attention to detail and ability to maintain confidentiality. Strong interpersonal and team work skills and ability to work with diverse groups. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Excel. Five years of progressively responsible experience in a related area within higher education. Knowledge of and affinity for design and planning professions is helpful. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover letter Three references Application Window Applications close on: October 18, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $21.63 - $23.56 hourly Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 58a6a2bb Last Name (required) 8eb3dd98 Email (required) 8bd20d68 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 5dd67213 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Architecture / Construction / Design Administrative / Professional Architecture / Construction / Design Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to yo