    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/physician-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Physician",
      "description": "Physician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Physician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Physician Apply Now Physician Lafene Health Center is looking for a highly dedicated and enthusiastic Sports Medicine Physician. 522232 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Lafene Student Health Center Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Oct 16 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position directly provides exceptional sports medicine and family practice healthcare services to eligible patients at Lafene Health Center and remote campus locations. The doctor will maintain a scope of practice contemporary to the needs of college health including diagnosis, treatment, and referral for consultation or specialty services, follow-up care, and serve as a positive and respectful resource to patients. Works cooperatively with the Lafene Health Center’s Medical Director, Administration, and all clinical and clerical staff in order to maintain a harmonious and productive work environment to the benefit of our patients. Works cooperatively with other Kansas State University departments to be a sports medicine and healthcare resource, as well as to provide care consistent with appropriate standards for sports medicine. Collaborating departments may include the K-State Athletics, Inc., Recreational Services, Department of Food, Nutrition, Dietetics and Health, etc. Provides clinical expertise in support of continuous quality initiatives, focused quality improvements and accreditation standards for Lafene Health Center. Other duties as assigned. About Us Lafene Health Center provides students with accessible, high-quality, and affordable outpatient healthcare, focusing on keeping students healthy and promoting a healthy campus community. Care is provided by board-certified physicians, nurse practitioners, and nursing professionals, ensuring students receive the same high-quality care they would expect from their healthcare providers at home. Students have access to coordinated and comprehensive services designed to build and maintain their overall well-being. We believe that good health is essential for academic success. The mission of Lafene Health Center at Kansas State University is to offer accessible, high-quality, affordable outpatient healthcare services on the Manhattan campus while also providing exceptional health and well-being education to the student body and the larger Kansas State University community. This mission is guided by the Health Center's core values of compassion, mutual respect, adherence to evidence-based healthcare and university standards, appreciation for timeliness, and collaboration, which ensures students receive respectful, efficient, and comprehensive care while fostering the best possible healthcare experience. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a doctorate degree in medicine and one year of relevant experience. Must be eligible to obtain a license to practice medicine in the state of Kansas. This position requires advanced medical knowledge and clinical training, which are most reliably developed through a doctorate in medicine—a prerequisite for medical licensure. Combined with at least one year of relevant experience, these qualifications ensure the candidate is prepared to deliver high-quality patient care, develop treatment plans, and collaborate effectively with medical staff. Preferred Qualifications: Treatment of sports related and/or musculoskeletal injuries and conditions. Board certified in Sports Medicine. Additional Role Information: Variable hours during evenings and weekends to provide coverage for athletic events and practices. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship 