    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-full-professor-manhattan-kansas-united-states-ace71d5d-bcc5-4a08-9a1f-5e89f6ffcd6c": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Apply Now Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Tenured or tenure-track faculty member with expertise in radiation protection. We are particularly interested in candidates with research backgrounds in nuclear lifecycle radiation safety, including front-end, operations, and/or back-end stages, though strong candidates in other areas of nuclear engineering may also be considered. 521873 Manhattan Alan Levin Dept Mech Nucl Engr Academic / Faculty - 9 month Closing at: Nov 15 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Alan Levin Department of Mechanical and Nuclear Engineering at Kansas State University is seeking applications for a faculty position in Nuclear Engineering. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain a strong, externally funded research program in radiation protection that complements the Nuclear Engineering Program's strengths and supports the University's focus on secure energy as an enabling technology. Additionally, the successful candidate will teach nuclear engineering courses and represent K-State through professional service in national and international roles. This recruitment is for a tenure-track, assistant professor, but highly qualified candidates may be considered at the level of associate or full professor. Tenure will only be considered for exceptional candidates. About Us The Nuclear Engineering Program has 8 faculty members, 2 staff members, and an enrollment of approximately 140 undergraduate and graduate students. K-State hosts a TRIGA Mark II Nuclear Reactor, with licensed thermal power level of 1.25 MW and pulsing capability. This growing program has garnered significant State and Federal investments and aims to become a Top 15 program by 2030. More information on the NE Program and the MNE department may be found at http://www.mne.ksu.edu . The Carl R. Ice College of Engineering is located on the main Kansas State University campus in Manhattan, Kansas, a vibrant, family-friendly city located in the scenic Flint Hills. Manhattan is the cultural and business hub of a tri-county area community of over 200,000 residents (for more information, see www.manhattan.org ). Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Nuclear Engineering, Health Physics, or a closely related field, from an accredited institution The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Nuclear Engineering with research backgrounds in nuclear lifecycle radiation safety Ability to develop strong externally funded research program in areas relevant to nuclear lifecycle radiation safety Active Certified Health Physicist Additional Role Information: Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, and continue through the application deadline of November 15, 2026. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Letter of application, CV, statement of research, Statement of teaching, and Contact information of five professional references Application Window Applications close on: November 15, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $125,000 - $175,000 annual salary Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) a80a0f2d Last Name (required) d77a9254 Email (required) 31e6ea09 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: d3e2b3d4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Engineering Research / Scientific / Grants Engineering Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 9 month Academic / Faculty - 9 month Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 7dea3ece Last Name (required) fd2a9602 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 8d9a1458 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) de249e5c Last Name (required) 3983dc50 Email (required) 20ce88ed Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 2b9fa015 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the 