      "description": "University Police Officer PT OJ - Manhattan, Kansas, United States University Police Officer PT OJ - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode University Police Officer PT OJ Apply Now University Police Officer PT OJ Temporary police officer for special events. 521889 Manhattan, Kansas, United States KSU Police Department Temporary Part-time Closing at: Dec 31 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Temporary part-time Police Officer to cover special events. Worksite Option This position is required to be performed on-site . Work is performed on employer premises or designated assignment location. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Completion of a basic law enforcement training program recognized by the Kansas Law Enforcement Training Commission One year of relevant experience in general law enforcement High school diploma Must possess a valid unrestricted driver’s license (corrected vision acceptable) upon employment Must be a United States Citizen and at least 21 years of age First Aid and CPR certification necessary within one year after employment Must hold a valid Kansas Peace Officer Certification in good standing prior to onboarding Must be certified by the Kansas Law Enforcement Training Commission within one year of employment and attend 40 hours of in service training each year after certification Must not have been convicted of and must be free of any diversions from a felony or a misdemeanor domestic violence crime Preferred Qualifications: Thorough working knowledge of local, state, and federal law, and university rules and regulations. Ability to make reports in written form in a clear and concise manner Additional special requirements preferred: (all of the following to be considered equally): expresses good judgment; displays job knowledge, skills abilities and interests; shows ability to maintain positive public relations; demonstrates analytical ability; demonstrates good verbal communication skills, indicates high stress tolerance Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume 3 professional references Screening of Applications Begins Immediately and continues until position is filled. Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $30.84 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 6e3b7314 Last Name (required) c2c63ab8 Email (required) 89d22476 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 442d0e1f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Law Enforcement Law Enforcement Employment Type Temporary Part-time Temporary Part-time Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 9a145874 Last Name (required) 48a62ae2 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 4fa3a401 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 033b5135 Last Name (required) 9d8590b0 Email (required) f02d6e73 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job dfed0480 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Cur