    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/academics-strategic-learning-post-graduate-intern-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Academics/Strategic Learning Post Graduate Intern",
      "description": "Academics/Strategic Learning Post Graduate Intern - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Academics/Strategic Learning Post Graduate Intern - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Academics/Strategic Learning Post Graduate Intern Apply Now Academics/Strategic Learning Post Graduate Intern Academics/Strategic Learning Post Graduate Intern: Responsible for providing academic support to a caseload of students that includes developing and monitoring academic plans, assisting with development of study skills and individualized learning strategies; assisting students with course and major selections, grade and eligibility requirements; connecting to tutorial and academic support resources; developing and maintaining academic records and reports, and other projects assigned by the fulltime staff. 521484 Manhattan, Kansas, United States K-State Athletics Inc (Agcy) Internship On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role K-State Athletics is seeking qualified applicants for an Academics/Strategic Learning Post Graduate Intern. This position is responsible for providing academic support to a caseload of students that includes developing and monitoring academic plans, assisting with development of study skills and individualized learning strategies; assisting students with course and major selections, grade and eligibility requirements; connecting to tutorial and academic support resources; developing and maintaining academic records and reports, and other projects assigned by the fulltime staff. About Us K-State Athletics, Inc. is a proud member of the Big 12 Conference and invites applicants who are passionate about collegiate athletics and want to become a member of our staff to help advance our department through hard work, knowledge, and dedication. Our mission is to foster a culture in which our student-athletes have every opportunity to reach their maximum potential academically, athletically, mentally and socially while operating an organization that is anchored by a genuine commitment to K-State, our supporters and each other. For more information on K-State Athletics, please visit https://www.kstatesports.com For more information on Manhattan, KS and the University, please visit https://www.k-state.edu/hcs/jobs/ Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree at time of application in higher education, special education, or related field Strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills with attention to detail Strong leadership capabilities Working knowledge of NCAA eligibility bylaws Must be able to work nights and weekends as required Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in higher education, special education, or related field Experience in student-athlete academic support / athletics academic services Experience working with at-risk student-athlete populations Experience working as GA in athletics academic support; in secondary or post-secondary education as a teacher or paraprofessional, or other related area Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply To be considered for the position, please complete the online application and submit/upload a current resume with three professional references and a letter of interest. Application Window Screening of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $12.50/hour (approx. 26,000 annually) plus paid overtime Benefits Excellent medical, dental, and vision plans Competitive retirement plan Earned vacation and sick leave plans Parental leave plan Term life insurance Accidental death and dismemberment insurance Long term disability insurance Paid KSU designated holidays K-State Athletics Local Agency Employee Benefits Information: https://www.kstatesports.com/sports/2020/3/6/athletics-human-resources.aspx?path=resources Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 22f42a78 Last Name (required) edc9a6f3 Email (required) 61b4db22 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 1a5617c3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Athletics Athletics Employment Type Internship Internship Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) d287d078 Last Name (required) b277632a Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later a1f13613 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 51d45eb2 Last Name (required) 0518035a Email (required) 78e9a5d7 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job ab51540a Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings 